\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Recent  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Aimed At Helping Smaller Exporters\b0\par\par\uc2 821 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2011\par 08:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appear aimed at helping smaller companies\par \par \uc2 -- Strategy of meeting all offers around Y79.20 helped exporters settle at favorable rates\par \par \uc2 -- Move appeared designed to avoid smaller companies getting shut out at best prices\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had an unusual feature--hours of calm as the dollar/yen rate flatlined just below Y79.20 through the afternoon session, a stark exception to the massive volatility that normally greets \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spending in the market of some Y7.5 trillion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The calm was no accident, however. It was a specific strategy employed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it continued to buy dollars during the Asian day, traders told Dow Jones Newswires.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The goal, they said, was to offer a helping hand to smaller exporters who are often locked out of fast-moving markets during periods of volatility as not all exporters can respond and call banks to place orders sufficiently quickly at the time of an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the rate steady for more than three hours, from 11:40 a.m. local time to 2:55 p.m. in Japan (0240 GMT to 0555 GMT), there was ample chance for smaller exporters to exchange their overseas earnings at a rate nearly 5% higher than would have been possible earlier in the day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ was like a giant on the ground catching all the meteorites falling out of the sky," said a senior dealer at a major bank in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thanks to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is almost certain to be a record for one day, many Japanese exporters secured the necessary funding arrangements for the current calendar year, traders said. That suggests fierce criticism over the strong yen and pressure to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from industry are less likely ahead, helping authorities avoid another major foray into the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the time, the move provoked speculation, especially among non-Japanese market participants, that Tokyo may be starting to imitate the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which is also fighting against a strong local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The SNB has effectively placed a floor for the euro against the franc and vowed unlimited \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect that level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chief Strategist Masafumi Yamamoto said, however, that it would be nearly impossible for Japan to adopt such a tactic, since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has only limited funds for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , unlike the Swiss. Many Japanese officials have also pointed out that it is unrealistic for Japan to create a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  floor given the huge market volume of dollar/yen trading.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts instead believe that the pinning of the spot took place because MOF wanted to give plenty of time for exporters to do whatever they needed at a favorable exchange rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In other recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaigns, not all exporters, especially those who aren't big players, were able to benefit from the improved rates during the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Minori Uchida, a senior analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  UFJ.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders also say only a limited number of exporters can act swiftly enough in the wake of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because staff at corporate treasury departments at many companies need to seek approval from senior managers to undertake \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions, a process that can take an entire day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "On Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , orders from Japanese exporters started to increase rapidly sometime after 1 p.m. (0400 GMT)," a trader said. He noted that the steady rate was maintained until just before the 3 p.m. (0600 GMT) deadline for Japanese firms to settle same-day spot trading, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So why Y79.20?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say that while the specific figure is still a mystery, for many exporters Y79.00 against the dollar is arguably the highest acceptable rate for the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Orders from Japanese exporters jumped once the dollar rose above Y79.00," a senior trader said. "And with 20 sen extra, they were able to trade year-end forward contracts at a rate above Y79.00."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders also argue that MOF likely stopped short of pushing the dollar above the psychological level of Y80.00 because it would have been too costly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Koji Fukaya, director of Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Research at Credit Suisse Securities in Japan, said short-term-focused speculators would have sold dollars more actively if the dollar had moved closer to Y80.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But traders discounted as a new urban myth a story making the rounds in Tokyo that the rate was due to a misunderstanding of comments from Finance Minister Jun Azumi. The story goes that Azumi, who said "nattoku iku made", meaning "until satisfied," was misunderstood to mean "Y79.19," which can be pronounced in a similar way in Japanese\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "That, of course, is a joke," said one trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 09-11-11 0756GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111109e7b9000nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
