\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Only On Aug 4 To Sell Dollars During Jul-Sep\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2011\par 02:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only on Aug. 4 during the July to September quarter, confirming market views that its efforts to cap the yen's rise in that period was limited to a one-day \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 According to the data for the July-September period, the ministry sold Y4.513 trillion for dollars on Aug. 4, which at the time was a record for the amount of yen sold in a single-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Aug. 4 yen sales pushed up the dollar over Y3 to above Y80, but the impact was quickly lost and the dollar fell to a then-record-low of Y75.94 on Aug. 19.\par \par \uc2 The ministry stepped in again on Oct. 31 after the dollar hit a fresh low of Y75.31 on that day, and sold an estimated Y7 trillion to Y8 trillion--a single day record--to weaken the yen and prevent it from sapping Japan's export-led economic rebound.\par \par \uc2 The chart below shows the amount spent on dollars and euros in each \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Date Amount \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bought\par \par \uc2 Aug 4, 2011 Y4.513 tln U.S. dollar\par \par \uc2 -By George Nishiyama, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2818; george.nishiyama@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111109e7b8000ya\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\