par \uc2 Traders in Tokyo said they have seen no evidence of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Oct. 31, which had started in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and continued during New York trading that day. There was a price spike during Asian trading on Nov. 1, but traders have attributed that move to dollar buying by Japanese banks acting on behalf of their clients, rather than renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 07-11-11 0442GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111107e7b70006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
