\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 4\b0\par\par\uc2 1,792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2011\par 08:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISOR: EU NEEDS EFFECTIVE BAILOUT PLAN BEFORE CHINA WILL GIVE MONEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Europe Union needs an effective bailout plan before China is willing "to give money", Li Daokui, an advisor to the People's Bank of China, said Friday. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBA KEEPS DOOR OPEN TO FURTHER CUTS; WARNS EUROPE IS MAJOR RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday left the door open to cut interest rates further over time, saying the biggest risk to the economy was Europe's sovereign debt crisis which is set to generate ongoing volatility for world financial markets. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN WARNS OF EUROPEAN HIT TO REVENUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan said Friday the ongoing debt crisis in Europe will hurt the government's total revenue, but reaffirmed a commitment to deliver a budget surplus in 2012-13. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER FURUKAWA VOWS VIGILANCE OVER ECB POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Friday he will stay watchful of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy, as changes in it affect economies elsewhere, including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM NODA EXPLAINS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , CONSUMPTION TAX HIKE PITCH TO G20 \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda cleared Japan's agenda at Thursday's Group of 20 nations meeting, explaining to the leaders of the world's major economies the reason for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and declaring the government's commitment to raise its consumption tax to rebuild its fiscal health. (published 0035 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA OFFICIAL: MONETARY POLICY TO BE MORE FLEXIBLE, FORWARD-LOOKING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's overall active fiscal policy and "prudent" monetary policy won't change next year, though monetary policy will have more flexibility and be forward-looking, a senior official said Friday. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: CAPITAL-ACCOUNT REFORM COULD SPEED UP YUAN RISE - \f28 \uc2 \f2 COMMERZBANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  ECONOMIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan's pace of appreciation is likely to speed up if Beijing accelerates its capital-account liberalization, a move that will increase capital inflows, Ashley Davies, a senior economist at Germany's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: YUAN HITS LOWER TRADING LIMIT AGAINST DOLLAR FOR 2ND STRAIGHT DAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan fell to its weakest permitted level against the U.S. dollar for a second straight day Friday, despite yet another record-high fixing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as investors continued to scramble for the safety of the greenback amid continued concerns about the health of China's economy and the euro-zone debt crisis. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOC HK CEO: OFFSHORE YUAN MARKET SLIGHTLY MORE MATURE THAN A FEW MONTHS AGO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The offshore yuan market has become more mature compared with a few months ago, with more "two-way traffic" in spot yuan trading, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOC Hong Kong Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive He Guangbei said Friday. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ICBC'S JIANG PLAYS DOWN PROPERTY FEARS, TIPS US QE3 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's top commercial banker said Friday that concerns over the health of the country's property market are exaggerated and that he expects a further round of quantitative easing in the U.S. to stimulate growth. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TAIWAN PROPOSES EASING RULES FOR BANKS TO INVEST IN YUAN PRODUCTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's financial regulator Friday proposed allowing the overseas units of Taiwanese banks to invest in government and corporate bonds traded in China--including those issued by non-Chinese entities--to broaden the investment channels of the banks as they struggle for growth in their home market. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA GOVERNOR: SEE ROOM TO CUT RATE ON TAME INFLATION OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Gov. Darmin Nasution Friday said inflationary pressure is likely to trend lower and create room for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to further cut its policy interest rate. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE OCTOBER CPI RISE FASTEST IN MORE THAN 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines accelerated in October to the fastest annual pace in more than two and half years, driven mainly by higher food prices as well as higher utility and services rates, official data showed Friday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: MALAYSIA SEPTEMBER EXPORTS +16.6% ON YEAR; +13.9% EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports grew a stronger-than-expected 16.6% on-year in September, helped by a sharp increase in shipments of palm oil, chemicals and chemical products and liquefied natural gas. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S SEPTEMBER TRADE SURPLUS TIPPED AT A$3B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia is expected to post a seasonally-adjusted September trade surplus of A$3.0 billion, down slightly from the A$3.1 billion posted a month before, according to the median forecast of a survey of 17 economists by Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA OCT NEW YUAN LOANS LIKELY ROSE; TRADE SURPLUS WIDENED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank lending in China likely increased slightly in October and the country's trade surplus likely widened, while money-supply growth was largely unchanged from the previous month, a Dow Jones Newswires poll of 12 economists indicated. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: KIRIN TO TAKE FULL OWNERSHIP OF BRAZIL'S SCHINCARIOL FOR $1.3B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kirin Holdings Co. said Friday it has bought all the shares it doesn't already own in Brazilian brewer Schincariol for around $1.3 billion, continuing its march into emerging markets after an unsuccessful attempt by Schincariol shareholders to block the deal. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: MF GLOBAL LIQUIDATORS SEE DEAL TO SELL ASIA-PACIFIC UNITS OVER WEEKEND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The liquidators of \f28 \uc2 \f2 MF Global Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Asia-Pacific units have received 30 to 40 credible purchase offers and the terms of a sale agreement may be reached over the weekend, said a KPMG spokeswoman in Hong Kong. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ 3RD UPDATE: TINGYI IN TALKS TO BUY \f28 \uc2 \f2 PEPSICO\f28 \uc2 \f2 'S BOTTLING OPS IN CHINA - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Instant noodle and beverage producer Tingyi Holding Corp. is in advanced talks to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 PepsiCo Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s bottling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in China in what marks the start of a partnership between the two companies, people familiar with the situation said Friday. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OLYMPUS DELAYS EARNINGS RELEASE, SHARES DROP 12% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will postpone the release of its fiscal second-quarter earnings, briefly sending its shares down 12% on the growing uncertainty created by questions about steep payments made in past acquisitions. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NIKON: THAI FLOODING TO LOWER REVENUE BY Y65B, OP PFT BY Y25B THIS FY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nikon Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . warned Friday that the flooding in Thailand would eat up a sizeable chunk of its earnings for the fiscal year ending in March. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOYOTA: TO EXTEND PRODUCTION CUTS AT JAPAN PLANT THROUGH NOV 12 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it will maintain production cutbacks in Japan and six other countries, mainly in North America and Southeast Asia, due to parts shortages resulting from the flooding in Thailand. (published 2359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: LENOVO EXECUTIVE: TO FOCUS ON LOW- TO MID-END PHONES IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese personal computer maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lenovo Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is focused on selling mobile phones in the low- to mid-range segments in China, Honorary Chairman and senior adviser \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liu Chuanzhi\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TEPCO GETS Y1 TRILLION BAILOUT TO HELP TACKLE NUCLEAR CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will receive about Y1 trillion in public funds to help it bear the weight of compensation claims from the Fukushima Daiichi crisis, as the struggling utility said it expects to go deep into the red for this fiscal year. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: QANTAS CEO JOYCE DEFENDS STRATEGY AT INQUIRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alan Joyce\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Friday told a public inquiry that proposed changes to aviation rules backed by unions and designed to stymie its Asian expansion would threaten the flag carrier's very survival. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PERENNIAL CHINA RETAIL TO BUYS 50% STAKE IN CHENGDU PROPERTY FOR CNY2.28B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Perennial China Retail Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  Friday said it plans to acquire a 50% stake in the Chengdu Longemont Shopping Mall Development in China for about CNY2.28 billion . (published 2359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BLACKROCK INC\f28 \uc2 \f2  BUYS 5% STAKE IN NEW ZEALAND'S TELECOM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investment management company \f28 \uc2 \f2 BlackRock Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  has taken a 5% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp of New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., according to a filing at the New Zealand Stock Exchange Friday. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BHARTI AIRTEL 2Q NET PROFIT DROPS 38%; MISSES FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday posted a disappointing 38% drop in second-quarter net profit as a weaker Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a surge in interest expenses drove up costs and its customers made fewer telephone calls. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOCAM DEVELOPMENT TERMINATES JV AGREEMENT TO BUY NANJING SITE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SOCAM Development Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has agreed to terminate a joint venture plan to buy a site in eastern China's Nanjing city for around CNY3.2 billion, because of China's tightening measures as well as rising uncertainties in global financial markets. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RIO TINTO CHAIRMAN SAYS CHINA ECON SLOWING BUT DEMAND STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chairman Jan du Plessis said Friday the Chinese economy is slowing visibly, but that strong domestic demand and manageable debt levels should make China's economy resilient to a "sharp correction" in the OECD economies. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES RISE AS GREEK WORRIES EASE; BANKS, RESOURCES GAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets climbed Friday, with financial and resources plays rallying as Greece's prime minister dropped plans for a referendum on the country's aid package, likely preventing the collapse of last week's eurozone bailout plan. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA OCTOBER COMMODITY IMPORTS MAY SOFTEN SLIGHTLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-11-11 0712GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's commodity imports likely eased slightly in October compared with September, but any declines may be limited by bargain hunting amid robust overseas supply, analysts said this week. (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL 2011-12 SUGAR OUTPUT FORECAST AT 173 MLN TONS, UP 4.1% ON YEAR -FAO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 World sugar production will likely rise 4.1% to 173 million metric tons this marketing year due to a significant expansion of cultivation area and increased fertilizer use, the United Nation's food body said. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 2011-12 RAW SUGAR OUTPUT TO RISE, BUT NEAR 20-YEAR LOW -ANZ \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The forecast is similar to an October output prediction by \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., but is below a September estimate of 4.2 million tons by the government's Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics and Sciences. (published 0339 GMT) [ 04-11-11 0712GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111104e7b4000mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
