\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Hot Stocks-GLP falls on weakening yen woes\b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2011\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 2 (Reuters) - Shares of Singapore-listed \uc2 Global Logistic Properties\uc2  (GLP) , which owns warehouses in China and Japan, fell as much as 2.6 percent on Wednesday, on concerns that a weaker yen as a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hurt its earnings.\par \par \uc2 At 0249 GMT, GLP shares were down 0.9 percent at S$1.71, with 2.1 million shares changing hands, underperforming the benchmark Straits Times Index's 0.15 percent loss.\par \par \uc2 "GLP has properties in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weakening. This could impact its bottom-line after translating its earnings in Japan back to Singapore dollars," said a local trader.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also concerned that GLP could be affected by slowing growth in China.\par \par \uc2 "Industrial activity is going down, which doesn't spell well for logistics," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Charmian Kok; Editing by Matt Driskill)\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE-MARKET-STOCKS/GLOBALLOGISTICPROPERTIES   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111102e7b20003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
