\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 2\b0\par\par\uc2 2,501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2011\par 08:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BOJ SHIRAI CONCERNED OVER IMPACT OF EURO CRISIS ON JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board member Sayuri Shirai said Wednesday that one of the most serious downside risks to the Japanese economy is the negative effects of the European sovereign debt crisis through "an international financial channel," indicating that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains on guard against potential economic impact from sharp market moves. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM: NEED TO BE ALERT OVER DOWNSIDE RISKS OF YEN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Wednesday that the government needs to be alert over possible downside risks posed by the yen's "one-sided rise" and reiterated that Tokyo will keep monitoring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements closely. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER: TOO EARLY TO SUMMARIZE EFFECTS OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Jun Azumi said Wednesday that it is too early to summarize the effects of Tokyo's recent yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA VICE FINANCE MINISTER: GLOBAL INFLATIONARY PRESSURES TO REMAIN HIGH IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China still faces many challenges, including rising protectionism, global inflationary pressures and the ongoing sovereign debt crisis in Europe, China Vice Finance Minister Li Yong said Wednesday. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA VICE FINANCE MINISTER: CHINA HAS STABILIZED PRICE INCREASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has stabilized price increases and the economy is moving in the right direction, China Vice Finance Minister Li Yong said Wednesday. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA OFFICIAL: INFLATION RISKS SUCH AS EXCHANGE-RATE VOLATILITY REMAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Vice Finance Minister Shin Je-yoon said the government remains committed to price stability despite easing inflation in October, citing risks such as exchange-rate volatility. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN URGES GREECE TO STICK WITH BAIL-OUT PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer Wayne Swan Wednesday criticised the Greek government's decision to hold a referendum on the nation's EUR130 billion bail-out plan and urged authorities to instead quickly implement the agreement struck by European leaders in Brussels last month. (published 0656 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA PRIME MINISTER: HAVE TO GUARD AGAINST IMPORTED INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India needs to guard against imported inflationary pressure as the euro-zone continues to reel under the debt crisis, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Wednesday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : 'IMPOSSIBLE' TO BE IMMUNE FROM GLOBAL SLOWDOWN AS EXPORTS FORM OVER 70% OF GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is impossible for Taiwan to be immune from a global economic slowdown as exports form 70% of the island's gross domestic product, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Perng Fai-nan told legislators Wednesday. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BANK INDONESIA OFFICIAL: ROOM FOR FURTHER RATE CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia sees room for further rate cuts after inflation eased in October, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Wednesday. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA'S ZHUHAI CITY IMPOSES CEILING ON HOME PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Zhuhai city in southern China's Guangdong province has set a ceiling of CNY11,285 per square meter for residential property transactions, becoming the first Chinese city to set a limit on residential property prices and triggering concerns of similar curbs in other cities. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: NEXT UP, A RATE CUT IN KOREA? NOT LIKELY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Countries in the Asia-Pacific region are starting to cut interest rates to buttress their economies against a global slowdown. Despite easing inflation and slowing growth in South Korea, the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't likely to be among the next to ease policy. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: PHILIPPINES OCTOBER CPI LIKELY UP 5.1% DUE TO TYPHOONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Supply shocks in the Philippines caused by several typhoons likely spurred inflation to a quicker pace in October, although economists doubt that higher consumer prices would force a policy tightening from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid dimmer global economic growth prospects. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREAN FIRMS MULL BID FOR ANGLO COAL MINE -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One of Australia's largest producing coal mines has attracted takeover interest from South Korea, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG International Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Electric Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Kepco, joining a consortium to consider a bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anglo American PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Callide mine, two people familiar with the matter said Wednesday. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA SLOWS RULING ON SHELL-PETROCHINA BID FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOW ENERGY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's foreign investment watchdog has pushed back a decision on the A$535 million takeover of coal seam gas developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bow Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by a joint venture of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by up to 90 days. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHOENIX SATELLITE TELEVISION PLANS TO SPIN OFF OUTDOOR MEDIA UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Phoenix Satellite Television Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to spin off its outdoor media unit Phoenix Metropolis Media Technology Co. on a technology- and growth-focused board of the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, the Hong Kong-based Chinese language Satellite TV operator said Tuesday. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SONY SINKS TO 2Q NET LOSS, SEES FY LOSS OVER $1B AS YEN, TV OPS WEIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it swung to a net loss for the three months ended Sept. 30 and now expects to lose well over $1 billion this fiscal year, as the strong yen dents sales outside Japan and its loss-making television business continues to struggle. (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MAZDA MOTOR SLUMPS TO 2Q LOSS, EXPECTS TO SHOW 4TH STRAIGHT FY RED INK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mazda Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it swung into the red in the July-September quarter, dragged down by the yen's surge and slumping sales, and said it now expects to make its fourth-straight full-year loss. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: VIRGIN AUSTRALIA TO MATCH QANTAS AS PRICE WAR LOOMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Virgin Australia Ltd. said Wednesday it will continue to compete aggressively on ticket prices with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . even if its rival pitches lower fares to win back customers lost through a damaging industrial dispute. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: DBS 3Q NET CLIMBS 6% ON STRONG LOANS GROWTH; BEATS EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Southeast Asia's largest bank by assets, Wednesday posted a better-than-expected 6% rise in third-quarter net profit as trade finance continued to drive the bank's loan growth. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WESTPAC FY NET PROFIT A$6.99B; FINAL DIVIDEND 80 CENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Westpac Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its full year net profit rose 10% helped in part by a decline in impairment charges, while the company signalled it will continue to be vigilant about costs in what it expects to be a subdued environment for credit growth. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WOOLWORTHS OUTLINES STRATEGY FOR NEW GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which runs Australia's largest supermarket chain, has outlined a new strategy to accelerate growth by opening new stores, creating 10,000 new jobs, embracing online platforms and updating its marketing. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TPV TECHNOLOGY HALTED FROM TRADING PENDING ACQUISITION ANNOUNCEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TPV Technology Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . were halted from trading from 0100 GMT, pending the release of details of a "very substantial acquisition", one of the world's biggest makers of computer monitors said Wednesday. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NUPLEX: COMPANY IS WELL POSITIONED TO DEAL WITH VOLATILE TIMES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Resins company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nuplex Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is well positioned to deal with uncertain and volatile times because of its geographical diversity, said Nuplex Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rob Aitken\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a speech to the company's annual general meeting. (published 2325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ONESTEEL\f28 \uc2 \f2  DROPS 16% AFTER IRON ORE, A$ HIT 1H OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in Australian steelmaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 OneSteel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . dropped 16% Wednesday after the company said first-half profits could fall by nearly 70% on the year, thanks to a sharp fall in the price of iron ore and the strengthening Australian dollar in recent months. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: QANTAS SEPTEMBER PASSENGERS UP 3.3%; LED BY JETSTAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . boosted passenger numbers by 3.3% in September compared with a year earlier as higher volumes at Jetstar offset the impact of strikes on its premium domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0108 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MIRVAC REAFFIRMS EARNINGS GUIDANCE AFTER POSITIVE 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property investor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mirvac Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Wednesday reaffirmed its full year earnings guidance after experiencing strong sales growth and high occupancy levels in its first quarter. (published 2224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK TELECOM\f28 \uc2 \f2 , KT TO LAUNCH APPLE IPHONE 4S IN SOUTH KOREA NOV 11 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's two largest mobile carriers by revenue, \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Telecom Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 KT Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Wednesday they will officially launch the latest version of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s iPhone 4S model in the Asian country on Nov. 11. (published 2347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAPURACREST\f28 \uc2 \f2  PETROLEUM: UNIT GETS $1.4 BLN CONTRACT FROM PETROBRAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SapuraCrest Petroleum Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s wholly-owned unit TL Offshore Sdn. Bhd. has received a contract worth $1.4 billion from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro S/A\f28 \uc2 \f2 , it said in an exchange filing late Tuesday. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KIA'S CHINA PRODUCTION CAPACITY TO JUMP 69% TO 730,000 UNITS/YEAR BY 2H 2014 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kia Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its annual production capacity in China will surge to 730,000 units by the second half of 2014 from 430,000 currently once its third plant in the country becomes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AU OPTRONICS: 16 SENIOR EXECUTIVES TO TAKE 15% PAY CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwanese flat-panel maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 AU Optronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said 16 senior executives will take a 15% pay cut from November, a move that came after the company posted a steep loss for the third quarter amid a supply glut of panels. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALIBABA GROUP: TO INVEST CNY1 BLN TO DRIVE TRAFFIC TO UNIT ETAO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-11-11 0718GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese e-commerce company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group Holding Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it will invest CNY1 billion to drive traffic to its eTao unit, an online-shopping search engine. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY DOWN ON GREEK WORRIES; TOKYO HITS 3-WEEK LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets dropped Wednesday, as Greece's plan to hold a referendum on its newly-crafted bailout package rattled investors, sending the Tokyo market to a three-week low and denting oil prices. (published 0506 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BY-PRODUCT OF NUCLEAR FISSION DETECTED AT FUKUSHIMA DAIICHI PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nuclear fission by-products have been detected at one of the reactors at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant, the government said Wednesday, raising the possibility that some parts of the melted core may still be active. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA MINE TAX HITS GAS SNAG AS REVIEW STARTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's 18-month drive to introduce a controversial new mining tax hit a fresh snag as it was introduced to parliament Wednesday, with a key independent lawmaker warning that he wouldn't support the law until further research was done on the environmental impact of the coal seam gas industry. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA SLOWS RULING ON SHELL-PETROCHINA BID FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOW ENERGY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's foreign investment watchdog has pushed back a decision on the A$535 million takeover of coal seam gas developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bow Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by a joint venture of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by up to 90 days. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA 2012 COPPER DEMAND UP 6.4% TO 7.85 MLN TONS -BEIJING ANTAIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's refined copper demand will likely rise by 6.4% to 7.85 million tons in 2012, according to the state-owned metals consultancy Beijing Antaike. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA COPPER DEMAND STILL STRONG; $7,000/TON SUPPORT -STANCHART \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese copper demand remains strong, as trading houses seek to increase sales to fabricators and consumption from air-conditioner manufacturers is likely to remain robust through the Lunar New Year in January, Standard Chartered said in a note Wednesday. (published 0240 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD MAY EXCEED USD2,000/OZ IF QUANTITATIVE EASING HAPPENS -BOFA MERRILl \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices may exceed $2,000 a troy ounce if the U.S. launches a fresh round of quantitative easing, a senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst said Wednesday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREAN FIRMS MULL BID FOR ANGLO COAL MINE -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One of Australia's largest producing coal mines has attracted takeover interest from South Korea, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG International Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Electric Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Kepco, joining a consortium to consider a bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anglo American PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Callide mine, two people familiar with the matter said Wednesday. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NATURAL RUBBER PRICES UNLIKELY TO FALL BELOW $3,500/TON THIS YEAR -EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber prices aren't likely to fall below $3,500 a metric ton this year, a senior Thailand-based industry executive said Wednesday. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par REGIONAL NATURAL RUBBER MARKET MAY BE SET UP IN AS SOON AS TWO YEARS -IRCO CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A regional natural rubber market that the International Rubber Consortium proposed just last year may be set up in as soon as two years, said the organization's chief executive Darmansyah Basyaruddin. (published 0037 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RIO TINTO BOOSTS DRIVERLESS IRON ORE TRUCK FLEET TO 150 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's second-largest iron ore miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  will boost its fleet of driverless trucks 15-fold to 150 vehicles over the next four years, as part of a bid to increase margins at its mines in Australia's Pilbara region. (published 0327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S ICBC OPENS PERTH BRANCH TO SERVICE MINING CLIENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial and Commercial Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest lender by market value, opened Wednesday its first office in Australia's resources hub Perth to service mainly mining clients. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TIRE OUTPUT TO GROW 6% IN 2011, SLOWER THAN 2010 -ASSOCIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's tire output will grow 6% in 2011, slower than 10% growth seen in 2010, according the deputy secretary general of the China Rubber Industry Association. (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAILAND MAY NOT MEET RUBBER TREE PLANTING TARGET -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rubber tree plantings in Thailand may not meet an official target as the government may divert funds to recover from recent floods, a senior Thai rubber official said Wednesday. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA NATURAL RUBBER IMPORTS TO INCREASE TO 425,000 TONS IN 2015 -EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's natural rubber imports are likely to increase to 425,000 metric tons in 2015, according material from a presentation due to be delivered later Wednesday but made available to delegates at an industry event Tuesday. (published 0018 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WHOLE-MILK POWDER PRICES RESUME SLIDE IN FONTERRA'S AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whole-milk powder prices eased 0.8% in New Zealand's dairy giant Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. overnight Internet-based auction, resuming their slide after rising slightly in the prior auction two weeks earlier. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FOOD MINISTER: INDONESIA WANTS TO IMPORT 500,000 TONS OF RICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia wants to import 500,000 tons of common-grade rice from India on a government-to-government basis, Food Minister K.V Thomas said Wednesday. (published 0527 GMT) [ 02-11-11 0718GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550