\par\par \b \uc2 KASB Securities Limited and Economics Research- Commodities Corner\b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2011\par \uc2 Pakistan Business News\par \uc2 ASBUSN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011. Asianet-Pakistan   \par \par \uc2 Gold Spot\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Japan intercepted the rise of the Yen for the third time this year, subsequently strengthening the USD and pushing gold prices lower.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 From a technical perspective, gold\u8217\'20\'19s Stochastic Oscillator has now generated a sell signal in the overbought region.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The first support is at $1,698.86 and second support is at $1,679.58. The first resistance is at $1,730.05 and the second resistance is at $1,747.92.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosts greenback, gold descends\par \par \uc2 According to KASB Securities, in an attempt to curb the rapidly appreciating Japanese Yen and combat speculation, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The USD/JPY fell as low as 75.50 and after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shot up to 79.50. The subsequent strength in the greenback pushed gold prices lower and further chipped away the gains of the precious metal which it had accumulated over the previous week. The remainder of the week will likely be dominated by outcomes of policy meetings of the Fed and the ECB in addition to G20 meetings scheduled for Nov 3?4.\par \par \uc2 Technical Strategy: Sell\par \par \uc2 Gold registered a lower high and a lower low to close below the 50?DMA. This confirms the view of a top while also suggesting further downside risk. The Stochastic Oscillator has now generated a sell signal in the overbought region while the RSI too has shown weakness and is on the verge of generating a sell signal. The first support is at $1,698.86 and second support is at $1,679.58. The first resistance is at $1,730.05 and the second resistance is at $1,747.92.\par \par \uc2 WTI Spot (Crude Oil)\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Oil endured a choppy trading session slipping to record a red closing as a stronger USD pushed commodities lower.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 From a technical perspective, WTI\u8217\'20\'19s Stochastic Oscillator continues to hover in the overbought region and is likely to generate a sell signal.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The first support is at $92.36 and second support is at $91.34. The first resistance is at $94.02 and the second resistance is at $95.36.\par \par \uc2 Crude caves in to dollar strength\par \par \uc2 Oil endured a choppy trading session slipping to record a red closing as a stronger USD pushed commodities lower across the board (CRB Index ?3.23). Riskier asset classes also suffered (Dow Jones ?2.3%, S&P ?2.5%) as markets were rattled by a futures broking firm filing for bankruptcy protection. Investors will await the release of the ISM Manufacturing PMI for the month of October where the consensus estimate stands at 52.1. A reading >50 is generally indicative of improvement in business conditions.\par \par \uc2 Technical Strategy: Sell\par \par \uc2 WTI opened significantly lower, however recovered from thereon only to close in the red. The Stochastic Oscillator continues to hover in the overbought region while the RSI has started to stall and is on the verge of generating a sell signal. The first support is at $92.36 and second support is at $91.34. The first resistance is at $94.02 and the second resistance is at $95.36.\par \par \uc2 Silver Spot\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Silver\u8217\'20\'19s golden streak came to a standstill as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?led selling affected commodity markets after the Japanese government stemmed the rise of the Yen.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 From a technical perspective, silver\u8217\'20\'19s Stochastic Oscillator has now generated a sell signal in the overbought region.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The first support is at $33.62 and second support at $32.88. The first resistance is at $34.94 and the second resistance is at $35.63.\par \par \uc2 Silver halts a profitable run\par \par \uc2 Silver\u8217\'20\'19s golden streak came to a standstill as the metal dropped for the first time in seven sessions on a resurgent USD. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?led selling affected several commodities following \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curtail the rapidly rising Yen and commodities ended lower (S&P GSCI Index ?4.6).\par \par \uc2 Technical Strategy: Sell on Strength\par \par \uc2 Silver registered a lower high and a lower low to close in the red. This confirms the view of a top while also suggesting further pressure. The Stochastic Oscillator has now generated a sell signal in the overbought region while the RSI has started to show weakness and is on the verge of generating a sell signal as well. The first support is at $33.62 and second support at $32.88. The first resistance is at $34.94 and the second resistance is at $35.63.\par \par \uc2 Dokument ASBUSN0020111101e7b10000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
