\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ data suggests  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  sold record 7.7 trln yen in  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2011\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 1 (Reuters) - Money market data from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday suggested \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day may have totalled a record amount around 7.68 trillion yen ($98.5 billion).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled two days after the transaction and the BOJ's projection for Wednesday's money market conditions showed there will be 7.68 trillion yen in payments to banks from the public sector.\par \par \uc2 Estimates from Japan money brokers surveyed by Reuters indicated there would likely be no net payment from the government to banks apart from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related transactions.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, it would surpass the record 4.5 trillion yen of yen-selling when Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Aug. 4.\par \par \uc2 The Asahi newspaper reported earlier that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reached 10 trillion yen ($128 billion).\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will officially announce on Nov. 30 how much it spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October. ($1 = 77.975 Japanese Yen)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Antoni Slodkowski; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \h