\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  During New York Trade Monday Confirmed - Sources\b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2011\par 07:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  orders during New York hours in addition to Asian trade on Monday, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in and outside of Asia said the MOF conducted the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  via EBS.\par \par \uc2 While the timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't known, EBS charts show the dollar rose steadily from around 1210 GMT, climbing to Y78.35 from Y77.92 over a 10-minute period. The rate remained steady at around the Y78.00 level until 1800 GMT, with another smaller rise around that time to Y78.18 at 1945 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimate the total amount of Japan's Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is between Y7 trillion and Y8 trillion. Though the amount the MOF sold the yen during the New York time is unknown, dealers said at the end of Asian trade on Monday that they believe the MOF sold well more than Y7 trillion.\par \par \uc2 It is not unusual for the MOF to continue its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign after Asian trading. In the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market believes the MOF placed orders during European hours though it didn't trade during New York time.\par \par \uc2 As of 0550 GMT, the dollar was at Y78.12.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, 