\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2011\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA CUTS CASH RATE TARGET 25 BPS TO 4.50% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  responded Tuesday to sharply reduced inflation risks and cut official interest rates by one quarter of a percentage point to 4.50% from 4.75%. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA OCTOBER PMI +5.1 POINTS TO 47.4 POINTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's manufacturing sector contracted at a slower pace in October but the sector continues to hurt from the strong exchange rate and weak demand, a performance gauge produced by an industry group published Tuesday shows. (published 2230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN NEW HOME SALES FALL 3.5% IN SEPTEMBER VS AUGUST -HIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian new home sales fell 3.5% in September from August to their lowest level since December 2000, sending a powerful signal to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  that key parts of the economy are in need of an interest rate cut. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA 3Q HOUSE PRICE INDEX FELL 1.2% VS 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The weighted average price of established houses in Australian capital cities fell 1.2% in the third quarter from the second quarter, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said Tuesday. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA OFFICIAL OCTOBER PMI FALLS; OUTLOOK UNCERTAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's official Purchasing Managers Index fell sharply in October contrary to expectations for a third consecutive increase, suggesting Beijing's tight monetary policy and weakening demand for its exports have started to weigh on growth in China's manufacturing sector. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HSBC CHINA OCTOBER PMI 51.0 VS PRELIMINARY 51.1, SEPTEMBER'S 49.9 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The final HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index, a gauge of nationwide manufacturing activity, rose to 51.0 in October compared with 49.9 in September, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESIDENTIAL PRICES FALL 0.23% IN OCTOBER VS SEPTEMBER; BIGGEST DROP THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Residential property prices in 100 major cities in China fell 0.23% in October from the previous month, the biggest decline this year and following a 0.03% on-month slide in September, China Real Estate Index System said Tuesday. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN THREATENS FURTHER YEN ACTION, SEEKS G-20 SUPPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A day after ordering a massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister threatened further action Tuesday, saying he will make "appropriate decisions" at the right time if speculators again push the yen sharply higher, hurting Japanese exporters. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER: TO CONTINUE TAKING DECISIVE STEPS ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister Motohisa Furukawa said Tuesday the government remains poised to conduct further yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves abruptly and appears to be driven by speculation. (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ OCT 6-7 MINUTES: SOME SAID DOWNSIDE RISKS TO ECON INCREASED FROM SEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some members of the Bank of Japan's policy board said downside risks to the Japanese economy had increased somewhat compared with the period considered at the September meeting, with one member maintaining that further monetary easing might be needed, according to minutes of the Oct. 6-7 policy board meeting released Tuesday. (published 0014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA OCTOBER EXPORTS WEAKEST IN 2 YEARS; INFLATION SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's October exports growth slumped to a two-year low while inflation for the month fell within the Bank of Korea's target band for the first time this year, underscoring increasing growth risks for Asia's fourth-largest economy as the world braces for a potential global slump. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  OCTOBER PMI 43.7 VS 44.5 SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Taiwan Purchasing Managers Index fell to 43.7 in October from 44.5 in September, as new domestic and export orders fell substantially, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0204 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MF GLOBAL SUSPENDED FROM CME CLEARINGHOUSE - CME CLEARINGHOUSE PRESIDENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exchange-operator CME Group Inc. suspended MF Global Inc. from CME's clearing house in connection with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Securities Investor Protection Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . investigation of the troubled brokerage and clearing firm. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RAILWAY MINISTRY TO SELL CNY30B BONDS NEXT WEEK - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Railways plans to sell CNY30 billion worth of bonds overseen by the country's top economic planning agency next week, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0119 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-11-11 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111101e7b10008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
