\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely To Pale Vs Swiss Efforts\b0\par\par\uc2 970 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2011\par 02:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Doubts remain about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to keep yen from strengthening again\par \par \uc2 --Japan is unlikely to emulate Swiss success in countering safe-haven demand\par \par \uc2 --Japan is too big to copy Swiss steps, analyst says\par \par \uc2 --Inflation is tying the hands of Japan's authorities, strategist says\par \par \uc2 By William L. Watts\par \par \uc2 A multitrillion-yen jolt of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a Monday morning is guaranteed to get traders' attention, but doubts remain over Tokyo's ability to keep the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening again.\par \par \uc2 A massive round of yen selling by the Bank of Japan on behalf of the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall sharply to a three-month low versus the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The greenback, which had hit a new post-World War II low in Asian action, jumped as high as Y79.53 from around Y75.77 ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar remained substantially higher versus the yen at Y77.99, but was significantly off its immediate post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the BOJ appeared to sell around Y7 trillion ($90 billion) or more of yen, although estimates varied.\par \par \uc2 Japan, however, is unlikely to emulate the success enjoyed so far by Switzerland, which has aggressively sought to counter safe-haven demand for its franc by placing a floor on the euro/Swiss franc exchange rate at 1.20 francs, strategists said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB, which expressed fear of deflation due to the strength of the franc, threatened to defend the line with unlimited quantities of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases. Markets view the threat as credible, strategists say. The September move by the SNB sent the euro soaring from near CHF1.10 to more than CHF1.20.\par \par \uc2 The euro traded Monday at CHF1.2179.\par \par \uc2 Japan's move was the latest salvo in what's become a solo effort by Japan to cap the strength of the yen amid fears the strong, safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is undercutting exporters and damaging the Japanese economy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August in a solo effort. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  delivered an effective dose of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, following a devastating earthquake and the Fukushima nuclear crisis.\par \par \uc2 But appetite for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the U.S., Europe and other trading partners facing soft economic outlooks of their own, quickly faded.\par \par \uc2 And with Japan unwilling or unable to take a page from the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's book, authorities may find themselves capable of providing only a short-lived respite from yen strength, strategists said.\par \par \uc2 "They haven't implemented a floor or set capital controls, unlike the Swiss, which is why this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be as effective," said Kathleen Brooks, research director at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .com in London.\par \par \uc2 Japan is too big to emulate Switzerland's big steps, she said. If it were to follow the SNB, it would likely incur the wrath of the U.S. as well as Asian economies, all of whom are Japan's major trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Ulrich Leuchtmann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 , said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy of sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be undermining its credibility. That's because its moves to contain the yen's rise have been followed by phases in which it allowed the yen to rise beyond levels seen in previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This has resulted in a gradual erosion of credibility of the BOJ and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with every market participant knowing that post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels represent favorable opportunities to enter dollar/yen shorts," he said, in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The Inflation Worry\par \par \uc2 Inflation is tying the hands of Japan's authorities, Leuchtmann said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has no inflation worries, because the franc's sharp appreciation had led to deflationary risks for the Swiss economy. Therefore, boosting the monetary base isn't a worry for the SNB.\par \par \uc2 But while the Japanese economy has suffered from decades of deflationary pressure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears any rise in inflation expectations would boost the cost of financing Japan's debt by boosting inflation premiums on Japanese government bonds, Leuchtmann said.\par \par \uc2 Takuji Okubo, an economist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in Tokyo, said the pattern of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fits Japanese officials' rule of conduct for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is to "restrain the strength of the yen, but not to weaken the yen."\par \par \uc2 "The circumstances under which they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today fit the rule perfectly," he said. "This rule of conduct also dictates that the yen should not weaken too much because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 A dollar/yen exchange rate of Y76 appears to be the average break-even level for Japanese manufacturers, he said.\par \par \uc2 The yen's recent moves to new highs versus the dollar, meanwhile, have been more reflective of the weakness of the dollar rather than the strength of the yen, said Simon Derrick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York Mellon in London.\par \par \uc2 That's a sentiment underscored by the euro's ability to press above the $1.40 level versus the U.S. unit despite the ongoing turmoil in the euro zone as well as the pound's ability to hold near $1.60 despite a fresh round of quantitative easing by the Bank of England, Derrick noted.\par \par \uc2 That's because a recent warning by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke on the risk of deflation serves to underscore ideas the Fed may soon move to implement additional easing measures of its own beyond the so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 Operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Twist effort to swap shorter-dated securities for longer-dated ones, he said.\par \par \uc2 The potential for further Fed action means the yen is likely to rise further, Okubo agreed.\par \par \uc2 "From their rule of conduct in yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the next time they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , yen has to be stronger than where they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," he said.\par \par \uc2 --By William L. Watts; 415-439-6400; AskNewswires@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111101e7b10012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
