\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/MarketBeat: Tokyo is Making it Hard to Dump the Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Lauricella   \par \uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2011\par 02:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Many folks are medium- or longer-term bearish on the outlook for the dollar, especially with all the chatter about the Federal Reserve coming in with another round of easing. But the continued very real risk of a blow-up in Europe -- or elsewhere -- that sparks a frenzy of safe-haven dollar buying had made it a challenge to build a position that isn't at risk of getting blown out of the water.\par \par \uc2 And at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , they think the latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue as deemed needed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That, they say, has implications for safe-haven buyers of yen -- and therefore the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The endgame is that such actions could reinforce the USD being the 'risk off' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice. That is, if the market cannot buy CHF or JPY when market stress intensifies sharply, then it will pile into the USD in a more aggressive manner for liquidity. For example, when the SNB's floor in EUR-CHF was established and concerns over Eurozone sovereign risk remained very high, this proved to be a key tipping point for EUR-USD to fall sharply.\par \par \uc2 We have seen how there has been a rotation of the primary 'risk off' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. Before Japan's earthquake, it used to be the JPY was the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  most likely to benefit in a 'risk off' scenario. Then after Japan's earthquake, the CHF took that title but after the SNB's floor, the USD moved into that position. This does not mean the USD is a better safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market wants liquidity and during times of fear, it will shift into the USD.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111101e7b1000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
