\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely To Pale Vs Swiss Efforts\b0\par\par\uc2 974 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 17:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Doubts remain about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to keep yen from strengthening again\par \par \uc2 --Japan is unlikely to emulate Swiss success in countering safe-haven demand\par \par \uc2 --Japan is too big to copy Swiss steps, analyst says\par \par \uc2 --Inflation is tying the hands of Japan's authorities, strategist says \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By William L. Watts \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A multitrillion-yen jolt of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a Monday morning is guaranteed to get traders' attention, but doubts remain over Tokyo's ability to keep the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from strengthening again.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A massive round of yen selling by the Bank of Japan on behalf of the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fall sharply to a three-month low versus the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback, which had hit a new post-World War II low in Asian action, jumped as high as Y79.53 from around Y75.77 ahead of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The dollar remained substantially higher versus the yen at Y77.99, but was significantly off its immediate post-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  high.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the BOJ appeared to sell around Y7 trillion ($90 billion) or more of yen, although estimates varied.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan, however, is unlikely to emulate the success enjoyed so far by Switzerland, which has aggressively sought to counter safe-haven demand for its franc by placing a floor on the euro/Swiss franc exchange rate at 1.20 francs, strategists said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The SNB, which expressed fear of deflation due to the strength of the franc, threatened to defend the line with unlimited quantities of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases. Markets view the threat as credible, strategists say. The September move by the SNB sent the euro soaring from near CHF1.10 to more than CHF1.20.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro traded Monday at CHF1.2179.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's move was the latest salvo in what's become a solo effort by Japan to cap the strength of the yen amid fears the strong, safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is undercutting exporters and damaging the Japanese economy.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in August in a solo effort. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  delivered an effective dose of coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in March, following a devastating earthquake and the Fukushima nuclear crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But appetite for coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the U.S., Europe and other trading partners facing soft economic outlooks of their own, quickly faded.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And with Japan unwilling or unable to take a page from the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's book, authorities may find themselves capable of providing only a short-lived respite from yen strength, strategists said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They haven't implemented a floor or set capital controls, unlike the Swiss, which is why this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not be as effective," said Kathleen Brooks, research director at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .com in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan is too big to emulate Switzerland's big steps, she said. If it were to follow the SNB, it would likely incur the wrath of the U.S. as well as Asian economies, all of whom are Japan's major trading partners.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ulrich Leuchtmann, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strategy of sporadic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be undermining its credibility. That's because its moves to contain the yen's rise have been followed by phases in which it allowed the yen to rise beyond levels seen in previous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This has resulted in a gradual erosion of credibility of the BOJ and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with every market participant knowing that post-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels represent favorable opportunities to enter dollar/yen shorts," he said, in a research note. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Inflation Worry \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation is tying the hands of Japan's authorities, Leuchtmann said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The SNB has no inflation worries, because the franc's sharp appreciation had led to deflationary risks for the Swiss economy. Therefore, boosting the monetary base isn't a worry for the SNB.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But while the Japanese economy has suffered from decades of deflationary pressure, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears any rise in inflation expectations would boost the cost of financing Japan's debt by boosting inflation premiums on Japanese government bonds, Leuchtmann said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Takuji Okubo, an economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo, said the pattern of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fits Japanese officials' rule of conduct for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is to "restrain the strength of the yen, but not to weaken the yen."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The circumstances under which they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today fit the rule perfectly," he said. "This rule of conduct also dictates that the yen should not weaken too much because of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A dollar/yen exchange rate of Y76 appears to be the average break-even level for Japanese manufacturers, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's recent moves to new highs versus the dollar, meanwhile, have been more reflective of the weakness of the dollar rather than the strength of the yen, said Simon Derrick, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank of New York Mellon in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That's a sentiment underscored by the euro's ability to press above the $1.40 level versus the U.S. unit despite the ongoing turmoil in the euro zone as well as the pound's ability to hold near $1.60 despite a fresh round of quantitative easing by the Bank of England, Derrick noted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That's because a recent warning by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke on the risk of deflation serves to underscore ideas the Fed may soon move to implement additional easing measures of its own beyond the so-called \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Twist effort to swap shorter-dated securities for longer-dated ones, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The potential for further Fed action means the yen is likely to rise further, Okubo agreed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "From their rule of conduct in yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the next time they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , yen has to be stronger than where they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --By William L. Watts; 415-439-6400; AskNewswires@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 31, 2011 12:18 ET (16:18 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111031e7av005lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
