\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-LatAm  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  slide on yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 17:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen move boosts dollar against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Commodity prices fall on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Argentina ratchets up peso control amid capital flight\par \par \uc2 * LatAm \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  October gains intact after Friday losses\par \par \uc2 (Adds Mexican prices to close)\par \par \uc2 By Jeb Blount\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Oct 31 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened against the U.S. dollar on Monday, led by Mexico's peso and Brazil's real, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's appreciation against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The strengthening of the dollar after Japan's second yen-selling move in less than three months caused global stock and commodities prices to fall. For details see [ID:nL4E7LV0D4] [ID:nN1E79U0EA]\par \par \uc2 Among the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, all but five weakened and of those, all were unchanged or little changed from Friday. Four of the nine biggest losers on Monday were from important commodity producers -- Norway's krone, South Africa's rand, Brazil's real and Mexico's peso.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters/Jefferies CRB index <.CRB> of 19 of the most traded agricultural, energy and metals commodities fell 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 A weaker yen makes Japan's imports of iron ore, copper, oil, food and other important Latin America-produced raw materials more expensive, which could undermine demand for those products. Japan, the world's third-largest economy, is highly dependent on imports of raw materials.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has triggered a generalized dollar move across the board," said Nick Chamie, head of emerging markets research with \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto. "People are also concerned on how this will impact demand for commodities and an appetite for risk."\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=D2> <MXN=>, weakened 2.75 percent to 13.3694 per U.S. dollar, its biggest one-day loss in more than five weeks. Monday's slide trimmed one-month gains to about 3.7 percent in October, the first in six months and the biggest since September 2010.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> lost 1.29 percent to 1.7020. Despite Monday's loss, the real's nearly 10 percent gain in October was the largest one-month jump since April 2003. Of the 152 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Thomson Reuters, only the Ugandan shilling <UGX=> gained more than the real in October.\par \par \uc2 The gains in the peso and real in October came as European leaders moved to resolve a sovereign debt and banking crisis that threatened to choke off credit for governments, individuals and businesses.\par \par \uc2 The risk of a global downturn had led investors to sell emerging market assets, which are considered risky, for the safety of the dollar. Agreements aimed at resolving the European crisis announced last week sent investors rushing back to emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The rally ended with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move that also caused raw materials prices to fall.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso, though, may be set to post new gains.\par \par \uc2 The premium banks pay to buy dollar put options from Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to its highest level since the program was reactivated in early 2010 as local banks paid more for protection against peso gains. [ID:nMEX004080]\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA TIGHTENS CONTROLS\par \par \uc2 Argentina increased control of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, requiring all dollar purchases to get approval from tax authorities.\par \par \uc2 The move, coming only days after President Cristina Fernandez' Oct. 23rd commanding re-election and an order that exporters bring 100 percent of foreign sales and earnings back into Argentina, caused the supply of dollars to dry up.\par \par \uc2 To prevent the Argentine peso from weakening sharply as the supply of dollars shrank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $1.80 billion of foreign reserves in October, including $100 million on Monday. [ID:nN1E79U0EK]\par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso <ARS=RASL> was little changed from Friday at 4.2350 per dollar in the interbank market. In the the parallel market <ARSB=>, the peso rose 0.28 percent to 4.4825.\par \par \uc2 Local media said the government planned to deploy several thousand officials to enforce the new rules, which critics described as a scare tactic to cool demand for dollars among Argentines concerned that inflation is undermining the peso's value.\par \par \uc2 Some suggest that the country's true inflation rate may be double the 10.9 percent official rate. The International Monetary Fund and other international organizations have questioned the accuracy of Argentina's official statistics.\par \par \uc2 Inflation has eroded the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's competitive edge for exporters. Investors, small and large, expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow a faster pace of depreciation in the coming months to protect local industry. [ID:nN1E79R1LJ]\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City, Walter Bianchi, Jorge Otaola and Hillary Burke in Buenos Aires; Editing by Jan Paschal)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111103e7av00183\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
