\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 4- \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2  to tame soaring yen ahead of G20\b0\par\par\uc2 1,108 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 03:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with vice finance minister)\par \par \uc2 * Dollar jumps over 4 pct, biggest gain in 3 years\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says acted solo, no comment on size\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not over yet, Vice Finance Minister says\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes days before G20 summit\par \par \uc2 * Dealers say size seems similar to Aug. 4 yen-selling\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Antoni Slodkowski\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 31 (Reuters) - Japan sold the yen for the second time in less than three months after it hit another record high against the dollar on Monday, saying it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter excessive speculation that was hurting the world's No. 3 economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  vaulted the dollar more than 4 percent higher, which would mark its biggest one-day gain in three years, and Finance Minister Jun Azumi said Tokyo would continue to step into the market until it was satisfied with the results.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, his deputy later said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not over yet, when asked to assess its effects as the dollar began slipping from the day's high.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ceased yet," Fumihiko Igarashi told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Many market players voiced doubts the impact would last given that previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since September 2010 had failed to prevent the yen from resuming its rally and setting a series of all-time highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo's latest foray followed repeated warnings that its patience with the yen's strength was wearing thin, and came just days before the Group of 20 leaders' summit in Cannes, France.\par \par \uc2 The summit will focus on Europe's efforts to contain its sovereign debt crisis and avoid a repeat of the financial shock that roiled markets after the \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  collapse in 2008.\par \par \uc2 But Tokyo is keen to win G20 understanding that a strong yen is one challenge too many for an economy grappling with a nuclear crisis, a $250 billion rebuilding effort from a March earthquake and tsunami and ballooning public debt.\par \par \uc2 Japan also says investors buy the yen as a safe haven from the euro zone debt crisis and stuttering U.S. growth. It argues such demand has nothing to do with the fragile health of the Japanese economy.\par \par \uc2 "We started \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this morning in order to take every measure against speculative and disorderly moves and to prevent risks to the Japanese economy from materialising," Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda told parliament.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after the dollar touched a record low of 75.31 yen and pushed the world's main reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up past 79 yen. The dollar, however, slipped below 78 in European trade.\par \par \uc2 Japan's economy has been recovering from its post-quake recession with companies swiftly restoring production and supply chains and Tokyo has counted on reconstruction spending and robust emerging markets demand to sustain the momentum.\par \par \uc2 But the yen's climb has spurred policymakers to act.\par \par \uc2 MORE TO COME?\par \par \uc2 Noda, who took over as Japan's sixth premier in five years last month, served as finance minister in the previous cabinet and led three past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  between September 2010 and August, including joint action with G7 partners in March 2011. The September 2010 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first in six years.\par \par \uc2 Azumi said that while Japan acted solo on Monday, he remained in close contact with his international counterparts.\par \par \uc2 Several G20 nations, including \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports rival South Korea, have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently in markets. But \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under more scrutiny as an issuer of one of three global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and does not want to be labeled as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 Azumi has indicated after his past meetings with Group of Seven and G20 partners that they appreciated Japan's special circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Still, many voiced doubts about how long the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would last, including \uc2 Honda Motor\uc2  Chief Financial Officer \uc2 Fumihiko Ike\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Frankly, my reaction was: 'finally, they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' But I'm also aware that a solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a limited impact," he said. "Will we be able to keep these levels" I'm not at all hopeful."\par \par \uc2 Stock market investors showed a similar reaction, Koichi Ogawa, chief portfolio manager at \uc2 Daiwa SB Investments\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially boosted shares in exporters, helping push the Nikkei average to a three-month intraday high. However, the market closed down 0.7 percent.\par \par \uc2 "The Nikkei was still unable to hold any gains, showing that investors are not confident that the yen will remain down," Ogawa said.\par \par \uc2 Takuji Okubo, chief economist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in Tokyo, was equally sceptical. "I do think this is one of many \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come," Okubo told Reuters Insider.\par \par \uc2 Some, however, said Monday's action that followed Bank Of Japan's monetary easing last week, could keep the yen away from its peaks for quite some time.\par \par \uc2 "It was very good timing. The BOJ has prepared the ground by easing last week. Speculators' yen-buying position has piled up, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is most effective in such cases," said Yunosuke Ikeda, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nomura Securities.\par \par \uc2 BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa was also hopeful the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the finance ministry -- would have an impact.\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ strongly hopes that such moves will lead to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stability," he said in a speech.\par \par \uc2 Azumi would not comment on the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but one trader said the authorities were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  "quite persistently".\par \par \uc2 The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could match the 4.5 trillion yen ($59 billion) Tokyo sold on Aug. 4 in its biggest single-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far, said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even though the yen's exchange rate measured against a trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket and adjusted for inflation is not far from its 30-year average, its dollar rate is much stronger than that used by exporters in their earnings projections.\par \par \uc2 That has led to a flurry of warnings from car makers and electronic firms that they might be forced to move more production abroad to cope.\par \par \uc2 Chipmaker Elpida warned it might have to move production overseas and Honda's chief executive said earlier this month that the company would half exports from Japan over the next decade because of the strong yen.\par \par \uc2 Last Thursday, acting in part out of concern that such "hollowing out" of the industry could stunt Japan's recovery, the BOJ eased its monetary policy by boosting government bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 ($1=75.76 yen)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Kaori Kaneko, Hideyuki Sano and Chang-Ran Kim in Tokyo, Masayuki Kitano in Singapore; Writing by Tomasz Janowski; Editing by Neil Fullick and Alex Richardson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-YEN/ (WRAPUP 4, PIX)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111103e7av0003t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
