\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won falls as  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  curbs yen, bonds firmer\b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 01:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won dips on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1,100/dollar\par \par \uc2 * Bonds firmer as risk rally loses steam\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Joonhee Yu\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The South Korean won slid against the dollar on Monday, weighed down by a fall in local shares and the U.S. dollar spiking to a 3-month high against the yen following aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The won was quoted at 1,110.0 to the dollar at the end of domestic trade on Monday, compared with Friday's close of 1,104.9.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a session high of 1,100.0 near the market open, when dealers said they spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities engaging in dollar-purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the 1,100 barrier, closely mirroring \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action earlier in the day to drive down the yen.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Japanese finance minister Jun Azumi said Japan engaged in a solo effort to sell the yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, a move designed to counter speculative buying which is driving up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and adding extra pressure on an economy still recovering from the devastating earthquake in March.\par \par \uc2 Seoul shares surrendered early leads to end 1.1 percent lower at 1,909.03, as investors consolidated their gains after last week's breakneck rally.\par \par \uc2 "We expected the equities market to take a breather today but the gap was larger than most expected," said Lawrence Kim, a market analyst at \uc2 Woori Investment & Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In addition to investors cashing in on profits from recent gains, there still exists lingering uncertainty regarding troubles in the U.S. and European economies which are still not out of the woods yet," he added.\par \par \uc2 Treasury bonds prices were up as the rally in risky assets lost momentum and signs of jitters reappeared in the market following Italy's lacklustre bond sales and the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's warning of a possible mass exodus of foreign capital if the global economy deteriorated further.\par \par \uc2 Yields on the benchmark 5-year treasury bonds shed four basis points to 3.63 percent while 3-year treasury bond yields shed three basis points to end at 3.51 percent.\par \par \uc2 December futures on three-year treasury bonds <KTBc1> gained 0.15 points to trade at 104.04.\par \par \uc2 "The dip in equities provided some momentum in the bond market today, but it is still lacking in terms of a clear direction. The industrial output data released today was also a mixed bag of different signals, and assuming that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep the base rate frozen for the time being, bond prices will likely remain flat and move within a narrow range," said a local bond trader.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 1.04 trillion won worth of monetary stabilisation bonds (MSBs) via auction at an average rate of 3.49 percent.\par \par \uc2 Also, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it will hold a repurchase auction on Tuesday to buy back 2.4 trillion won worth of 2-year MSBs from bond holders ahead of their maturity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Close    Prev close\par Dollar/won            1,110.0       1,104.9\par Yen/won           14.0618/745   14.5618/722\par *KTB futures           104.04        103.89\par 5-yr treasury bonds  3.63 pct      3.67 pct\par 3-yr treasury bonds  3.51 pct      3.54 pct\par Average call rate    3.28 pct      -\par ^6-mth KORIBOR       3.63 pct      3.63 pct\par KOSPI                1,909.03      1,929.48\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Front-month futures on 3-year treasury bonds <KTBc1>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^ Korea interbank offered rate\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting By Joonhee Yu; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -BONDS (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111103e7av00012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
