\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen wary of more  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , euro sags\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 23:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Market waits to see if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again\par \par \uc2 * Dollar off peak vs yen, but still sharply higher\par \par \uc2 * Euro hammered by renewed debt worries\par \par \uc2 * China PMI, Australia rate decision in play\par \par \uc2 By Ian Chua\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The dollar pulled back slightly from a three-month peak against the yen on Tuesday as the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  faded a touch, while the euro came under renewed pressure amid growing doubts over a plan to contain Europe's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at 78.30 yen , having risen as much four big figures to 79.55 on Monday in the wake of a record one-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated by some market players to be anything from $90 billion to $130 billion.\par \par \uc2 The options market, however, showed bets on the yen's gains against the dollar on a one-month horizon had not eased significantly, reflecting the market's belief that the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not last more than a few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Steve Barrow, strategist at Standard Bank, said if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not repeated, just as the case back in August, then dollar/yen could quickly return to the 75 region.\par \par \uc2 "We feel that the BOJ needs to vary the tactics here and would be better served by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently in order to hang on to the gains it has made so far," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Even this tactic would not stop dollar/yen falling to our target of 70, but at least it might mean that this is a long-term possibility rather than a near-term probability."\par \par \uc2 One of the reasons supporting underlying demand for the yen is that it is the least unattractive among the G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indeed, despite last Thursday's euro zone summit deal, doubts about how those measures could be implemented continued to haunt the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 News that the Greek prime minister has called an unexpected referendum on a new EU bailout deal for his debt-ridden country coupled with persistent pressure on Italian bonds renewed worries about the region.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3840 , having reversed all of the gains to $1.4247 made last Thursday after the debt deal was announced.\par \par \uc2 "The depth and breadth of unanswered questions from Thursday's EU deal, the spectacle of euro-peripheral bonds yields/yield spreads mostly higher Monday and general support afforded the USD from the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ensured EURUSD traded down in fits and starts throughout Monday," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  analysts wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 Immediate support for the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at the overnight low of $1.3827, a level representing the 38.2 percent retracement of the October rally from $1.3144 to $1.4247.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coupled with renewed euro weakness saw the dollar index rally to 76.503, up 1.9 percent. That was the largest one-day gain since late 2008.\par \par \uc2 This move also weighed on commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Australian dollar fell to $1.0545 from the recent high of $1.0753.\par \par \uc2 The immediate focus for the Aussie is the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's rate decision due at 0330 GMT, where many analysts expect a 25 basis point rate cut following recent benign inflation data.\par \par \uc2 Should the RBA hold rates steady, the Aussie could regain some of the overnight losses, traders said. The market will also be keeping an eye on China's manufacturing data due around 0100 GMT for the latest signs of whether the world's second biggest economy is on track for a soft landing.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve starts its two-day policy deliberations later on Tuesday, while the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its meeting on Thursday, ahead of key U.S. jobs data on Friday.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Wayne Cole)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111031e7av0021e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
