\par\par \b \uc2 Europe Factors-Shares set to fall; miners seen under pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 1,160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds detail, company news; updates snapshot table)\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 31 (Reuters) - European shares are set to fall on Monday, with a sharp drop in metals prices on a firmer dollar following \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market seen hurting miners, and as investors are still waiting to see finer details of a euro zone rescue deal.\par \par \uc2  German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble was cited as saying in a magazine that Europe still has a long way to go to solve its crisis, noting it was key Italy did its homework and implemented promised reforms. \par \par \uc2  "As the European bailout plan is dissected, we are likely to get further updates on how flawed or iron-clad the plan actually is," Stan Shamu, strategist at IG Markets, said.\par \par \uc2  "Many feel that the mild interest in the Italian debt auction on Friday showed that bond investors are still sceptical that the EU debt deal will actually calm the crisis."\par \par \uc2  Italy's sale of 7.94 billion euros of government bonds met lower demand than at previous auctions and the country paid the highest premium since joining the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell 10-year debt.  \par \par \uc2  Futures for the Euro STOXX 50 <STXEc1>, Germany's DAX <FDXc1> and the French CAC 40 <FCEc1> fell 0.8 to 1 percent, pointing to a weaker start for equities. Financial spreadbetters earlier predicted Britain's FTSE 100 to open as much as 0.8 percent lower.\par \par \uc2  Investors' focus will be on a summit of the Group of 20 leaders, which will take place in Cannes, France, on Nov. 3-4. Spain and Portugal called for the United States and other G20 powers to take action at the meeting to help contain the fallout from the European debt crisis. \par \par \uc2  Mining shares are expected to come under pressure after copper prices\par \par \uc2 fell 2.8 percent, gold dropped 2 percent and zinc  declined 2.1 percent following a rise in the dollar after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. A stronger U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes dollar-priced metals costlier for the holders of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and lowers demand.  \par \par \uc2  Focus will also be on banks, which have suffered heavily this year on the euro zone debt crisis and a slow pace of global economic recovery. Accountants \uc2 Ernst & Young\uc2  said a sluggish economy will take its toll on Britain's key financial services sector next year, forcing banks to write off more loans and restricting the supply of credit to consumers and businesses \par \par \uc2  The FTSEurofirst 300 index of top European shares ended 0.2 percent lower at 1,018.14 points on Friday, but finished the week up 4.1 percent -- its biggest weekly gain since early October. The index, up 10 percent this month, is on course to record its best monthly gains since April 2009, but is still down 9 percent in 2011.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0726 GMT                                   \par                                            LAST      PCT CHG     NET CHG\par   S&P 500                       1,285.09       0.04 %         0.5\par   NIKKEI                       8,988.39      -0.69 %      -62.08\par   MSCI ASIA EX-JP                    -1.23 %       -6.21\par   EUR/USD                         1.4008      -0.98 %     -0.0139\par   USD/JPY                          78.94       4.24 %      3.2100\par   10-YR US TSY YLD            2.288           --       -0.04\par   10-YR BUND YLD              2.149           --       -0.05\par   SPOT GOLD                    $1,712.70      -1.54 %     -$26.74\par   US CRUDE           <CLc1>              $92.53      -0.85 %       -0.79\par \tab \par  * US STOCKS-Wall St, finishing flat, posts 4 weeks of gains \tab \par  * Dollar spikes vs yen on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Asian shares fall   \tab \par  * Oil prices slip; G20 meeting eyed                         \tab \par  * Copper rolls back gains as Europe deal euphoria           \tab \par  * Dollar hits 3-month high on yen as Tokyo steps in         \tab \par  * Gold slides 2 pct on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2  COMPANY NEWS\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  BARCLAYS \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported a 5 percent rise in underlying quarterly profit as lower\par charges for bad debt at the British bank offset a third consecutive sharp fall\par in investment banking revenues as the euro zone financial crisis deepened.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UNICREDIT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to launch a 5-billion euro rights issue to meet\par tougher European capital rules early next year if market conditions stabilise,\par according to bankers circling the lender for mandates. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  TNT EXPRESS \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Dutch freight and delivery firm TNT Express reported higher-than-expected\par third-quarter operating profit on Monday, in the wake of a profit warning issued\par earlier this month, and said it was looking for further cost cuts. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  GLENCORE  \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The commodity trader is no longer in talks to provide financing to\par Indonesian conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bakrie Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which is close to a deal on Monday with\par Indonesian investors to help avert a default on a $1.345 billion loan, two\par sources with direct knowledge of the deal said.  \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROYAL BANK OF SCOTLAND\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Private equity group \f28 \uc2 \f2 CVC Capital Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  has made an offer for the\par insurance arm of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Scotland\f28 \uc2 \f2  for about 4 billion pounds ($6.5\par billion), the Mail on Sunday reported. \tab \par \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  EDISON , A2A   \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Shareholders of Italian utility Edison have agreed to take more time to iron\par out the details of a deal hammered out on Thursday that will give French\par electricity giant EDF majority control of Italy's No.2 power generator,\par sources said. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    \tab \par  BT GROUP  \tab \par  Britain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 BT Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has brought forward by one year its target to roll out a\par fibre network, meaning two thirds of premises will have access to the superfast\par broadband by the end of 2014. \tab \par   \tab \par  EURO ZONE DEBT CRISIS  \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Markets have over-interpreted comments by incoming European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par chief Mario Draghi on the bank's readiness to go on buying the bonds of troubled\par euro zone states, outgoing ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said in an\par interview. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  CLARIANT  \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Swiss speciality chemicals maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clariant\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Monday it expected a\par further slowdown in economic activity after the strong Swiss franc weighed on\par profits. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   \tab \par  G4S   \tab \par  Two large shareholders in G4S -- Artemis and Schroders -- are set to vote\par against the security firm's 5.2 billion pound ($8.4 billion) deal for Danish\par outsourcing firm ISS ISSHOI.UL, the Sunday Telegraph reported. \tab \par \tab \par  GERMAN BANKS             \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Charles Dallara, managing director of the Institute of International\par Finance, told Welt am Sonntag he is very optimistic that more than 90 percent of\par banks will accept a 50 percent discount on their Greek debt holdings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    \tab \par  ALLIANZ  \tab \par  The German insurer will accept a 50 percent discount on its Greek debt\par holdings, its finance chief told an Austrian newspaper.  \tab \par  Separately, Tagesspiegel reported that Allianz and reinsurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Munich Re\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par            have not yet decided whether to buy more Greek government bonds.  \tab \par   \tab \par  VOLKSWAGEN            , PORSCHE              \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Sportscar maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Porsche AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to introduce one new model line a year to\par expand its lineup to seven lines from currently four, German magazine Focus\par cited \f28 \uc2 \f2 Porsche AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Matthias Mueller as saying. He also said there\par were no plans for an electric version of the Porsche 911 model. Related news\par [VOWG_p.DE-E] [PSHG_p.DE-E]    \tab \par \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Atul Prakash)\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EUROPE-FACTORS  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111031e7av000m7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
