\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Tumbles As Debt Worries Return;  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 22:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The euro experienced its biggest single-day percentage drop against the dollar in more than a year, as jitters about the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis resurfaced.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given back all of its gains since Thursday, when European leaders announced a plan to stabilize the region's financial system. The agreement aims to boost the euro-zone bailout fund's firepower, cut Greece's debt load and recapitalize the region's banks.\par \par \uc2 While billed as a "comprehensive package," market watchers say the region's leaders still have many details to hammer out, and implementation will be tricky.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, fears that a Greek default could drag down Italy and other European economies remained in full force, weighing down the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the euro was at $1.3858 from $1.4147 late Friday, its biggest one-day percentage decline since August 2010, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 "We're getting a dose of reality," said Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 . "Now people are focusing on the fine print and there's a lot of uncertainties in that fine print."\par \par \uc2 The euro's swoon came alongside a jump in 10-year Italian government bond yields, which rose above 6%. Meanwhile, European stocks, including shares of many of the region's top banks, sank. \uc2 BNP Paribas SA\uc2  fell 9.6% and \uc2 Societe Generale SA\uc2  slumped 9.8% in Paris. The costs to insure European sovereign debt also rose. On Monday, the five-year credit default swap spread on Italy was 45 basis points wider at 447 basis points, according to data provider Markit.\par \par \uc2 Investors got another jolt late Monday following reports that Greece's government would hold a referendum on the newly minted aid package, and would also hold a vote of confidence on the government. Such developments add another layer of uncertainty for the debt-ridden country and for the euro zone's ability to dig its way out of the ongoing crisis.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the euro's woes was a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese government to weaken the Japanese yen. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent an estimated Y7 trillion, about $90 billion, to cap a rise in the yen that has undermined the economy and made exports less competitive abroad. That gave the dollar a boost against the yen, rising to Y78.17 from Y75.83. The euro was at Y108.34 from Y107.29.\par \par \uc2 The dollar and the yen have been among the favored safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent market volatility. But the threat of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the yen leaves the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice in times of risk aversion, giving it additional momentum against the euro and other growth-sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier Monday, Japanese Finance Minister Jun Azumi reiterated the government will continue to take "decisive steps" against "speculative movement in the market." But analysts say it will be difficult for Japan's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop general market trends, which continue to lean toward a stronger yen.\par \par \uc2 Among other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.K. pound was at $1.6082 from $1.6129. The dollar was at CHF0.8765 from CHF0.8629. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at about 76.484 from about 75.067.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com [ 10-31-11 1719ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111031e7av0007j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
