\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Jolts Markets; Euro Crisis Back On Agenda\b0\par\par\uc2 772 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 13:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse yen strength, sells an estimated Y7 trillion\par \par \uc2 --Relief over the euro zone's latest debt crisis plan wanes, Italian 10-year bond yields above 6%\par \par \uc2 --Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure, Hungarian forint sharply lower\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eva Szalay \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON -(Dow Jones)- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  jolted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Monday with a round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in what is thought to be one of the biggest dollar-buying efforts on record, while the euro fell below $1.40 after five-year Italian government bond yields touched a euro-era high.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is thought to have spent around Y5 trillion-Y7.5 trillion ($60 billion-$80 billion) to buy dollars against the yen, pushing the pair up to Y79.55 in an effort to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the greenback printed another record low against the yen at Y75.31 at the start of Asian trading hours.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be far more difficult to explain away to developed country peers, as volatility hasn't been anywhere near as high as in the previous efforts," said Derek Halpenny, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi-UFJ in London. "The trigger seems to have been the spot [rate] approaching the Y75 level."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Halpenny said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be an effort by the country to get leaders of the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations to discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issues when they gather for a summit on Nov 3-4. Despite Japan's heavy-handed attempt to reverse yen strength the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered off its session lows against the dollar in European trading hours.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market chatter warning of dollar-buying orders left by the Bank of Japan in the market around the Y78.90 and the Y78 levels proved unfounded, allowing the market to probe lower and lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Japanese authorities appear to have limited their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to an initial spurt at the market open," UBS AG said in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the European crisis rose back up the agenda, after Italian 10-year bond yields breached the 6% level once again after China said at the weekend that it wouldn't ride to the euro zone's rescue and plug the financial hole needed to implement the resolution plan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As we had expected, the euphoria following the summit outcome last week has not lasted very long," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note to clients. "It is becoming obvious already that the implementation bears risks and difficulties."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In emerging markets, the Hungarian forint came under heavy pressure and the euro ticked above HUF305 for the first time since April 2009, as concerns about Hungary's credit rating and heavy exposure to Swiss-franc mortgages weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Norwegian krone also came under selling pressure after retail sales data from the country disappointed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1126 GMT the dollar was trading at Y77.94 after hitting its highest level against the yen since Aug 4 at Y79.55, compared to Y75.83 in New York late Friday, according to EBS via CQG. The euro was trading at $1.4013 compared to $1.4147, while it was trading at Y109.17 from Y107.29. Sterling was at $1.6018 from $1.6129.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index was at 75.932 compared to 75.088.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1124 GMT     1.4005     77.89      1.6013     0.8714 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish    Bearish    Range      Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.3963     79.54      1.6006     0.8814 \par 3rd Resistance    1.4172     80.50      1.6211     0.8881 \par 2nd Resistance    1.4133     79.55      1.6150     0.8823 \par 1st Resistance    1.4054     79.14      1.6075     0.8769 \par Pivot*            1.4160     75.83      1.6118     0.8626 \par 1st Support       1.3974     77.65      1.5967     0.8673 \par 2nd Support       1.3955     77.48      1.5931     0.8612 \par 3rd Support       1.3921     76.60      1.5850     0.8568 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/JPY \par  \par Spot 1124 GMT     109.08 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish \par 200 day ma        111.03 \par 3rd Resistance    111.67 \par 2nd Resistance    111.57 \par 1st Resistance    110.90 \par Pivot*            107.42 \par 1st Support    