\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Keeps Dollar At Y79.20\b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 07:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen continuing, pinning dollar at Y79.20\par \par \uc2 -- Focus now is whether Japan will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London, New York markets\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar was pinned at Y79.20 for most of Asian trading on Monday as Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen aggressively swallowing dollar-selling orders by short-term-focused investors and Japanese exporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier in the day, Finance Minister Jun Azumi confirmed that Tokyo started its latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaign at 0125 GMT, and dealers said the authorities were still actively buying dollars in afternoon trading.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After hitting a session high at Y79.55, the greenback stayed at Y79.20 from 0240 GMT. It was at Y75.65 before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You see the line is flat in the dollar/yen EBS chart but that's not because the system is broken," a senior dealer at a major Japanese bank said. In fact, the flow of dollar/yen trading is well over five times larger than average, according to data from EBS.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Short-term-focused speculators and Japanese exporters were selling the dollar, the senior dealer said, adding "the fact the greenback isn't falling despite these orders means someone has been there to buy the U.S. unit at Y79.20."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo traders said the authority's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been very powerful and that the total amount of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen to have exceeded August's Y4.5 trillion, reaching Y6 trillion for a record-high figure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Koji Fukaya said the timing of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was surprising and it is likely that the effect of the latest campaign will last longer than it did in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, investors will pay attention to whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market in London and New York later in the global day, and in Tokyo on Tuesday, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Okasan Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  senior dealer Tsutomu Soma.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another focus will be a Federal Open Market Committee meeting later this week, said Nomura Trust and Banking senior dealer Hideki Amikura. He said if the Fed takes additional easing actions and shares fail to rise much, the dollar may resume falling despite Japan's efforts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0550 GMT, the dollar was at Y79.20, almost unchanged from Y79.21 at 0305 GMT. The euro was at Y110.94 and $1.3993 while the ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 76.227.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 0150 EST / 0550 GMT \par  \par                          Latest         Previous  %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par                                         2150 GMT           High     Low    12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            79.19-20       75.64-66  +4.69    79.55    75.58  -2.37 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.4009-12      1.4135-50  -0.93   1.4170   1.3988  +4.63 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5981-86      1.6120-34  -0.89   1.6133   1.5968  +2.41 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.8724-28      0.8620-36  +1.14   0.8737   0.8612  -6.67 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.0014-18      0.9919-22  +0.96   1.0026   0.9917  +0.69 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0534-38      1.0710-14  -1.64   1.0712   1.0508  +2.95 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8104-10      0.8226-30  -1.47   0.8227   0.8080  +3.98 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan           110.94-98      106.89-07  +3.72   111.53   107.02  +2.14 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 10-31-11 0246ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111031e7av0001m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
