\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par EURO-ZONE UNEMPLOYMENT HITS NEW RECORD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of unemployed people in the euro zone hits a new record in September after the biggest month-to-month rise in unemployment in two years, adding to concerns about the region's economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALIAN BONDS BREACH 6% YIELD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian government bonds buckle, with five-year yields climbing to euro-era highs and the 10-year yield rising above the psychologically important 6% level as the post-European Union summit enthusiasm in risky assets fizzles out.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN SAYS DEFICIT TARGET AT RISK AS GROWTH FLATLINES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says that growth in the euro zone's fourth-largest economy flatlined in the third quarter, signalling a growing threat that the country's government may miss a closely-watched deficit reduction target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TNK-BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  EYES STAKE IN HRT'S AMAZON OIL BLOCKS FOR $1B \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TNK-BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  will pay $1 billion to buy a stake in exploration blocks in the Amazon region from Brazil's HRT, the Brazilian company says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD SEES WEAK GROWTH UNTIL 2013 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Advanced economies are looking at two years of weak growth and high unemployment, and the outlook is likely to worsen unless the euro zone fails to reign in its sovereign debt crisis, the OECD says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BARCLAYS REVENUE BEATS ESTIMATES AND PEERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bob Diamond\f28 \uc2 \f2  says he is "absolutely committed" to a goal to hit a 13% return-on-equity target by 2013, despite a decline in investment-banking revenue this year that analysts fear could stall the plan's timeline.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB WEIDMANN CASTS DOUBT ON EURO-ZONE MEASURES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governing Council Member Jens Weidmann douses hopes that the latest set of measures adopted to resolve the euro-zone crisis could alone resolve the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  block's debt and banking woes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER; FOCUS ON EUROPE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock index futures fall, pointing to a lower start for Wall Street, with markets taking a cue from Europe as the initial euphoria surrounding last week's plan to contain the euro-zone debt crisis fades and investors are left looking for more details.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STAGES RECORD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government launches a fresh round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , spending an estimated Y7 trillion to cap a rise in the yen that has undermined the economy and dragged down the key export sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIA MAY PROVIDE $10B TO EURO-ZONE BAILOUT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's chief presidential economic aide says that Moscow is ready to help the euro zone solve its debt crisis by providing up to $10 billion through the IMF, shying away from bilateral contributions to a special European stability fund.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Focus \par DID THE EURO'S ARCHITECTS EXPECT IT TO FAIL? \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Could it be that those who designed the structures of the euro zone always knew they were flawed, but reasoned that a structural breakdown would enable them to bring in the common fiscal policy that would otherwise have been politically impossible?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par GETTING MORE BANG FROM TOKYO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday is like using a water pistol to put out a forest fire. Japan could get more bang for its buck by focusing on Europe instead.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DJ Newswires Survey \par CREDIT SUISSE EARNINGS SEEN POOR, MAY CUT MORE JOBS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to join peers in reporting dismal third-quarter earnings from its investment bank Tuesday, when the Swiss bank may also announce more job cuts and further restructuring as it strives to cope with tough markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Money Talks \par IGNORE EQUITIES, WATCH BONDS. AND WORRY. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In amongst the equity market's euphoria of the past few weeks, bond investors have been distinctly less enthusiastic. Not only didn't they participate in the general cheer, but they are growing downright gloomy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER; FOCUS ON EUROPE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures lower with focus on Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US TREASURYS PARE BACK RECENT LOSSES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US Treasurys pare recent losses as euro zone debt comes under renewed selling pressure.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  KEEPS DOLLAR AT Y79.20 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar is pinned at Y79.20 for most of Asian trading as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE FALLS ON STRONGER DOLLAR; FOMC, ECB IN FOCUS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude remains lower as profit-taking continues on a stronger dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD DOWN ON USD RALLY; OUTLOOK SEEN FIRM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold lower in Europe amid downward pressure from a stronger dollar. [ 31-10-11 1200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av001ew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
