 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BCS) 3Q Earnings \par Due: Oct 31, at 0700 GMT \par DJ Survey of 3 Analysts \par Average Pretax Profit (ex own-debt gains): \par GBP920M, down 28% (GBP1.27B in 3Q 2010) \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  Revenue: \par GBP2.10B, down 26% (GBP2.83B in 3Q 2010) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  will be the main focus, as usual, with revenues seen sharply off versus prior quarters as the euro-zone debt crisis put a lid on client activity. Analysts are looking for clarity around costs, with several expecting cost-to-income in the investment banking division to be above 70%, higher than the bank's 60%-65% guidance for the full year. Other targets, such as an aim for a 13% return on equity by 2013, will also be questioned in light of changing business and regulatory conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Clariant\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CLN.VX) 3Q Earnings \par Due: Oct. 31 at 0600 GMT \par DJ Survey of 5 Analysts \par Average Net Profit: CHF34.2M, -68%  (CHF106M in 3Q 2010) \par Average Sales:      CHF1.77B, +3.6% (CHF1.71B in 3Q 2010) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clariant\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to experienced a slightly deteriorating market environment overall in 3Q due to weakening demand and a high Swiss franc. However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  situation has substantially improved since the company's profit warning on Sept. 5. Although 3Q results are seen as rather poor, analysts will look for a guidance upgrade which could prove a positive trigger for the stock. The company is also expected to report a positive acquisition impact mainly from the purchased Sued-Chemie business. [ 31-10-11 1123GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1011   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av001d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
