\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS: European Stocks Fall; Resources Weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 10:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --European stocks in the red; resources under pressure\par \par \uc2 --Investors skeptical about EU deal\par \par \uc2 --Worries about growth also weigh\par \par \uc2 --Dollar up vs yen after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Michele Maatouk\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--European stocks fell Monday, with basic resources pacing the decline, as doubts crept in about the effectiveness of the European Union's summit deal.\par \par \uc2 "The program still lacks clear details regarding the technicalities of the different measures," said brokerage Newedge.\par \par \uc2 At 0850 GMT, the benchmark Stoxx Europe 600 index was down 0.9% at 246.82. London's FTSE 100 index was 0.9% lower at 5649.88, Frankfurt's DAX was 1.1% lower at 6276.43, and Paris's CAC-40 was down 1.4% at 3301.36.\par \par \uc2 Basic resources were the biggest drag, with the Stoxx Europe 600 index for the sector down 1.8%, as key metals prices fell. The two other mains cyclical sectors also suffered heavy losses. The Stoxx Europe 600 autos index was down 1.8%, while the index for banks dropped 1.5%.\par \par \uc2 Apart from a lack of detail, one of the biggest problems with the EU package is that it largely depends on the ability to attract non-European investment, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "Having apparently exhausted its own financial resources, Europe's desperate overtures to the likes of China or the International Monetary Fund will not be heeded without costs," said FxPro. "Both have expressed only lukewarm interest thus far, keen to avoid a situation where they lose control of how the funds are spent and on what terms," it said.\par \par \uc2 "Both the IMF and China may well come to the party, but it will be on their terms and will not be cheap, either financially or politically," added FxPro.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, worries about a slowdown in growth continued to play on investors' minds.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  Monday cut its euro-area GDP forecast for 2012 to +0.2%, from a previous estimate of +1% and said it now expects a recession in the first half of 2012. "The downward revision for 2012 is large, particularly when considering that we cut our forecast by a full percentage point just two months ago," said \uc2 UBS\uc2 . It cited credit tightening as the chief reason for the downgrade and said recent surveys and anecdotal evidence point to a sharp downturn in conditions.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, investors will eye Thursday's European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate announcement - Mario Draghi's first meeting as ECB President - as well as the G-20 summit, which takes place in Cannes on the last two days of the week.\par \par \uc2 On Monday's economic calendar, U.K. mortgage approvals are at 0930 GMT, euro-zone flash inflation estimates and unemployment data are at 1000 GMT, while in the U.S., the Chicago purchasing managers index is at 1345 GMT.\par \par \uc2 In Asia, stock markets were lower Monday, with shares in Tokyo choppy as the yen tumbled following Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Australia's S&P/ASX 200 fell 0.8%, South Korea's Kospi Composite lost 0.9%, Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index declined 1.1%, and China's Shanghai Composite Index was 0.5% lower. Japan's Nikkei Stock Average was volatile on confirmation of the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and fell 0.2% after climbing as much as 0.8%.\par \par \uc2 At 0855 GMT, the dollar was at Y77.91 from Y75.83. Earlier in the Asian trading day, the dollar fell to a post World War II record low of Y75.31, a move that prompted the Japanese government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the euro was at $1.4007 against the dollar, from $1.4147 late Friday in New York.\par \par \uc2 In other asset classes, spot gold was at $1,715.20 per troy ounce, down $28.30 from its New York settlement Monday. December Nymex crude oil futures were down 68 cents at $92.64 a barrel and Brent oil futures were down 50 cents at $109.41. The December bund contract was up 0.64 at 134.31.\par \par \uc2 -By Michele Maatouk, Dow Jones Newswires; +44-20-7842-9447; michele.maatouk@dowjones.com [ 31-10-11 0918GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1106   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av0015a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
