\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 31\b0\par\par\uc2 1,906 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 08:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 4TH UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STAGES RECORD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , PUSHES DLR UP 5% AT PEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government launched a fresh round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday, spending an estimated Y5 trillion-Y6 trillion to cap a rise in the yen that has undermined the economy and dragged down the key export sector. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF CONTINUES TO REMAIN IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET - 3 SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market after staging a dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier Monday, three people familiar with the matter said. (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM NODA: CONDUCTED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO WARD OFF ECONOMIC DOWNSIDE RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Monday that his government conducted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the day to ward off damage to the export-driven economy from the yen's strength, which he said was due to speculative moves. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN PLEDGES SUPPORT FOR EFSF, AFTER CHINA DEMURS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of a European bailout fund on Monday won assurances that Japan will continue to invest in the beefed-up European Financial Stability Facility to help tackle the continent's debt crisis, providing some welcome news for the fund after China made no commitment to invest. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA PRESIDENT: G-20 TO DISCUSS WAYS TO STABILIZE, STIMULATE GLOBAL GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders attending the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations summit in Cannes this week will discuss ways to stabilize and stimulate global economic growth, President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono said Monday. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA RATE CUT ON EDGE AS CREDIT GROWS STRONGLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian credit growth was strong in September, adding to evidence of a modest pick-up in the commodity-rich economy over recent months and ensuring any decision by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates on Tuesday will be tight. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN SEPTEMBER CAPITAL-CITY HOUSE PRICES DOWN 0.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian capital-city house prices continued to fall in September, with a recent rebound in the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worrying brokers that the steady declines in the market so far this year could continue. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA SAYS 3Q INDICATORS WEAK DESPITE STRONGER SEP OUTPUT DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Monday said economic momentum deteriorated during the third quarter despite better-than-expected industrial output growth in September, but reiterated the government will do its best to meet its 2011 economic growth target of 4.5%. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER LI: CHINA INFLATION TO DROP TO 2.8% IN 2012 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer price index growth may drop sharply to 2.8% in 2012, the Beijing Times reported Monday, citing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTER: EXPECT INFLATION TO MODERATE FROM DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation rate is expected to ease from December, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Monday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA OFFICIAL OCTOBER PMI LIKELY UP AT 51.7 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's official purchasing managers index, a gauge of manufacturing activity, likely rose in October, further alleviating concerns over a slowdown in the world's second-largest economy. (published 0352 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: HK SEPTEMBER RETAIL SALES GROWTH LIKELY STEADY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's retail sales continued to increase at a steady pace in September, underpinned by spending by visitors from mainland China, but the recent correction in financial markets might hurt consumer sentiment in the months ahead, economists said. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA OCT CPI LIKELY +4.80% ON YEAR, +0.17% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's on-year inflation rate accelerated slightly to 4.80% in October from 4.61% in September because of a low base of comparison, according to a median forecast of nine regional economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA SEPTEMBER TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY $2.72 BLN VS $3.76 BLN AUG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's trade surplus in September likely fell sharply from August, because of weaker prices for nearly all its export commodities, economists said. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: QANTAS RESUMES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AFTER DISPUTE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Qantas Airways sent a plane aloft Monday, hours after a government tribunal ordered an end to a destructive industrial dispute that grounded its fleet. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WIPRO TOPS FORECAST; REVENUE, VOLUME DRIVE SHARES UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wipro Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday posted a better-than-expected 1.2% rise in quarterly net profit from a year earlier and robust revenue and business volume growth sequentially, as its restructuring of the division that writes computer codes and provides technology services has started showing results. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QUANTA COMPUTER 3RD-QUARTER NET PROFIT DOWN 6.7%, GROSS MARGIN UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Quanta Computer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s third-quarter net profit fell 6.7% from a year earlier, it said Monday. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COMPAL ELECTRONICS JANUARY-SEPTEMBER NET PROFIT DOWN 53% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Compal Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its January-September net profit fell 53% from a year earlier. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CAPITAMALL TRUST\f28 \uc2 \f2  SEEKING TO RAISE UP TO S$300 MLN VIA PRIVATE PLACEMENT - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CapitaMall Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  is looking to raise up to S$300 million through a private placement for asset enhancement and to meet its capital expenditure needs, a person familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHI-X LAUNCHES IN AUSTRALIA AS ASX LOSES MONOPOLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The first rival stock exchange in Australia to ASX Ltd. officially launched Monday, although brokers noted sparse action on the new exchange in its first day. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HARVEY NORMAN 1Q GLOBAL SALES EXCLUDING SINGAPORE A$1.48B, DOWN 3.8% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Harvey Norman Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday blamed a strong Australian dollar, price deflation and competition for an expected 19.3% fall in first quarter profit. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GREAT EASTERN HOLDINGS\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q NET PROFIT FALLS 76% ON INVESTMENT LOSSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Great Eastern Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that its third-quarter net profit fell 76% due to investment-related losses in the quarter. (published 2337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANVIL MINING: RISK THAT MMR DEAL MAY FAIL ON GECAMINES OBJECTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The C$1.33 billion cash bid for Africa-focused copper miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anvil Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by Chinese mining investor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Minmetals Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . may fail because of objections from the Democratic Republic of Congo's state-owned mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gecamines\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Anvil said Monday. (published 2332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FUJIFILM 1H SALES, PROFITS DOWN ON STRONG YEN, CUTS FY OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fujifilm Holdings Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that its sales and profits for the first half ended Sept. 30 declined from a year earlier, blaming the negative effect of the yen's strength and higher costs of raw materials. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TENCENT DEVELOPING NEW WAYS TO OVERSEE MICROBLOG CONTENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tencent Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is developing new ways to oversee content on its Tencent Weibo microblog service as the company faces demands from China's government and from society to prevent the spread of rumors online, Tencent Chairman Pony Ma said Monday. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOHU.COM 3RD-QUARTER NET PROFIT UP 14% AT $46.8 MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Internet portal \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sohu.com Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its third-quarter net profit rose 14% from a year earlier because of strong advertising and online gaming revenue growth. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES DOWN; NIKKEI CHOPPY, YEN FALLS AS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were lower Monday, with shares in Tokyo choppy as the yen tumbled after Japanese authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MAY NEED TO RESTART NUCLEAR PLANTS TO SAVE COSTS -FORMER IEA HEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan may need to bring more of its nuclear power plants back online by early next year to save on fuel costs, Nobuo Tanaka, the former executive director of the International Energy Agency said Monday. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI RICE EXPORTERS DECLARE FORCE MAJEURE ON SHIPMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai rice exporters have declared force majeure on shipments of several thousand tons due to disruptions caused by heavy floods, trading executives said Monday. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CISA: HIGHER-THAN-USUAL LEVEL OF STEEL OUTPUT CUTS LIKELY IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's steel output will likely fall more steeply than usual for this time of year in the fourth quarter, China Iron and Steel Association Vice Chairman Zhang Changfu said Monday. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA BAOSTEEL: IRON ORE PRICES REACH A TURNING POINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iron ore prices have reached a turning point due to recent global economic turmoil and a slump in the Chinese steel market's, an executive of China's leading steelmaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Baoshan Iron & Steel Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GDF SUEZ\f28 \uc2 \f2 : MAY LOOK AT JOINT PROJECTS, SUPPLY DEALS WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , PETROCHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GDF Suez SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the French power and gas company, said Monday that it has had contact with oil and gas companies such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Petroleum & Chemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Sinopec, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . about working together on LNG projects. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAP OIL: RECEIVES SEVERAL ENQUIRIES ABOUT AUSTRALIA GAS BLOCK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tap Oil Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it will consider selling its 10% stake in the Zola gas discovery offshore Western Australia before any liquefied natural gas development occurs, and has already received several enquiries about its plans. (published 2305 GMT Sunday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GDF SUEZ\f28 \uc2 \f2 : TO COOPERATE WITH CNOOC ON OFFSHORE LNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-10-11 0725GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GDF Suez S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the French power and gas company, said Monday it will provide \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Offshore Oil Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd. with a vessel to store and regasify liquefied natural gas offshore. (published 0221 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE EMA TO STUDY ELECTRICITY IMPORTS BY END-2011 -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's Energy Market Authority will begin public consultations over a regulatory framework to govern electricity imports to the city-state by end-2011, Minister in the Prime Minister's Office S. Iswaran said Monday. (published 0204 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CISA: DISCUSSING PRICING SYSTEM REFORM WITH MINERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has been discussing reform of the way iron ore is priced with global miners, but has so far left Chinese steelmakers to work out their own contracts for the raw material, a senior China Iron and Steel Association official said Monday. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: RAIN SLOWS EARLY WESTERN AUSTRALIAN WHEAT HARVEST -CBH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The early stage of a harvest of winter grains--including wheat--in Western Australia is suffering conditions similar to the devastating conditions that severely harmed grain quality in the eastern states a year ago, a key grain logistics manager said Monday. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA GOLD DEMAND FELL DURING PEAK FESTIVAL SEASON - WORLD GOLD COUNCIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold demand in India fell during the peak festival season over the past one month as high inflation and tight household budgets dented consumer spending, the World Gold Council said Monday. (published 0709 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA 2011-12 SUGAR OUTPUT SEEN AT 24.7 MLN-25 MLN TONS - FOOD MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's sugar output in the marketing year that began Oct. 1 may rise to 25 million metric tons, Food Minister K.V. Thomas said Monday. (published 0708 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHANGHAI GOLD EXCHANGE: JP MORGAN CHINA BECOMES EXCHANGE MEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase Bank Co. has become a foreign financial member on the Shanghai Gold Exchange, the bourse said Monday in a statement on its website. (published 0707 GMT) [ 31-10-11 0725GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av000tx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
