\par\par \b \uc2 Australian Dollar Down Late After  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 06:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                            Rates At 0523 GMT \par                            Latest       Change \par  AUD/USD                   1.0532        -1.4% \par  AUD/JPY                   83.411        +2.9% \par  6.50% May, 2013           4.0%          -0.04 \par  4.50% Mar, 2020           4.4395%       -0.03 \par  10-Yr Spread To U.S.      +222 bps      -7 bps \par  SFE Dec 3-Year Futures    96.08         +0.04 \par  SFE Dec 10-Year Futures   95.455        +0.03 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--A massive effort by Japan to weaken its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rattled markets Monday, sending the Australian dollar lower against the greenback but higher against the yen ahead of a crucial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Although \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders suspect the effort was likely bigger than previous episodes.\par \par \uc2 "We think the size could be as large as or even larger than the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  strategists.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar tumbled to a low of US$1.0509 from an early high of US$1.0709. At 0523 GMT, the Australian dollar was at US$1.0532 from US$1.0677 late Friday. Against the yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed hands at Y83.411 from Y81.025.\par \par \uc2 The week ahead poses plenty of event risk. Locally, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  meets on Tuesday and is widely tipped to lower its interest rate in what would be its first adjustment in 12 months. If the RBA does cut, dealers will be closely looking for any signal that the easing is a one-off or the start of a trend.\par \par \uc2 The bigger risk is that the bank holds rates steady at 4.75%, said \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2  strategist Joseph Capurso. He said the focus will soon swing from domestic action to the G-20 leaders meeting this week, while a meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also be in focus.\par \par \uc2 "Over time, we expect the optimism that Europe can manage its public debt-banking crisis to wane. This should put downward pressure on the Australian dollar. However, in the near term, positive announcements from the G-20 meeting this week are likely to support the Australian dollar," said Capurso.\par \par \uc2 Emma Lawson, strategist at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 , said the disruption of Qantas flights over the weekend was a slight negative for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the margin.\par \par \uc2 "However, the resumption of flights and a near-term resolution to the industrial action may temper the broader negative sentiment from the weekend," she said.\par \par \uc2 -By Enda Curran, Dow Jones Newswires; 61-2-8272-4687; enda.curran@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Data provided by Reuters) [ 31-10-11 0542GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1054 22765 4109   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av000gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
