\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Dollar/Yen Options Up As  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 05:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options rose in Tokyo Monday as the Japanese government conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing the underlying exchange rate up sharply and prompting investors to seek protection against sharper moves.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark one-month at-the-money dollar/yen volatilities rose to 9.80%/10.40% as of 0200 GMT from 9.50%/10.00% late Friday in New York. The rise came after Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordered the Bank of Japan to sell yen in the market, a move which pushed the greenback up from around Y75.65 to a high of Y79.55.\par \par \uc2 The large jump, which was the highest since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on August 4, fueled demand for hedges against volatile moves in the spot market, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 At 0415 GMT, the dollar traded hands at Y79.18.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the higher dollar level dented demand for hedges against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downside, limiting the overall rise in option prices, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    1 Month Option Implied Volatilities At 0200 GMT \par  \par               Tokyo           New York        Tokyo \par               Monday          Friday          Friday \par Dollar/Yen    9.80%/10.40%    9.50%/10.00%    9.97%/10.37% \par Euro/Dollar   12.85%/13.35%   12.85%/13.35%   13.13%/13.88% \par Euro/Yen      13.80%/14.75%   13.80%/14.75%   14.52%/16.02% \par  \par  \par    3 Month Option Implied Volatilities \par  \par               Tokyo          Tokyo \par               Monday         Friday \par Dollar/Yen    10.05%/10.45%  10.29%/10.69% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volatilities used are over-the-counter, at-the-money rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1-month 25 delta risk-reversals favor dollar put/yen call options by 0.30%/0.90% compared with 0.05%/1.18% in Tokyo Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Monahan, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2783; andrew.monahan@dowjones.com [ 31-10-11 0417GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1077 4127   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av000bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
