\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TO CAP STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government launched a new round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday, moving to cap a continued rise in the yen that is undermining the economy and dragging down the key export sector. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR SURGES AS TOKYO STEPS IN TO WEAKEN YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar stormed back against its rivals Monday as Tokyo launched a new round of dollar-buying to weaken the yen. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF CONTINUES TO REMAIN IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET - 3 SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market after staging a dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier Monday, three people familiar with the matter said. (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVT FUJIMURA: ONE-SIDED YEN RISE WAS RISK TO JAPAN ECON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Monday that the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the morning was intended to prevent a downturn in Japan's economy due to the yen's dramatic rise against the dollar. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA SAYS 3Q INDICATORS WEAK DESPITE STRONGER SEP OUTPUT DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Monday said economic momentum deteriorated during the third quarter despite better-than-expected industrial output growth in September, but reiterated the government will do its best to meet its 2011 economic growth target of 4.5%. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA RATE CUT ON EDGE AS CREDIT GROWS STRONGLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian credit growth was strong in September, adding to evidence of a modest pick-up in the commodity-rich economy over recent months and ensuring any decision by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates on Tuesday will be tight. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN SEPTEMBER CAPITAL-CITY HOUSE PRICES DOWN 0.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian capital-city house prices continued to fall in September, with a recent rebound in the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worrying brokers that the steady declines in the market so far this year could continue. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER LI: CHINA INFLATION TO DROP TO 2.8% IN 2012 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer price index growth may drop sharply to 2.8% in 2012, the Beijing Times reported Monday, citing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF OFFICIAL: JAPAN TO CONTINUE TO BUY EFSF BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior official from the Japanese finance ministry said Monday that the country will buy more bonds from the European Financial Stability Facility, but may not maintain the same purchasing rate. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA PRESIDENT: G-20 TO DISCUSS WAYS TO STABILIZE, STIMULATE GLOBAL GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders attending the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations summit in Cannes this week will discuss ways to stabilize and stimulate global economic growth, President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono said Monday. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SHANGHAI TO SELL CNY7.1B BONDS IN NOVEMBER - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The municipality of Shanghai plans to directly sell CNY7.1 billion worth of local government debt in November, in the largest such debt offering this year, three people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOC HONG KONG SEEKS PRICE 5-YEAR DOLLAR BONDS TO YIELD AROUND TSYS +290BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOC Hong Kong Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to price an issuance of five-year, U.S. dollar-denominated bonds at around 290 basis points over comparable Treasurys, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA OFFICIAL OCTOBER PMI LIKELY UP AT 51.7 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's official purchasing managers index, a gauge of manufacturing activity, likely rose in October, further alleviating concerns over a slowdown in the world's second-largest economy. (published 0352 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(10/31) HEARD ON THE ST: WALL STREET REAPS PROFIT VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Here's a pop quiz: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the third quarter generated: a) 56 cents a share in earnings, b) 27 cents, c) a loss of two cents, or d) all of the above. (published 0136 GMT) [ 31-10-11 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av000ak\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
