\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 656 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET TO CAP STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government launched a new round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday, moving to cap a continued rise in the yen that is undermining the economy and dragging down the key export sector. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVT FUJIMURA: ONE-SIDED YEN RISE WAS RISK TO JAPAN ECON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Monday that the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the morning was intended to prevent a downturn in Japan's economy due to the yen's dramatic rise against the dollar. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JCR AFFIRMS JAPAN AAA RATING; SAYS TIME FOR FISCAL ACTION IS GETTING SHORTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Credit Rating Agency has affirmed its triple-A rating of the Japan sovereign, but urged the government to move swiftly on fiscal consolidation, especially tax increases. (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF OFFICIAL: JAPAN TO CONTINUE TO BUY EFSF BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior official from the Japanese finance ministry said Monday that the country will buy more bonds from the European Financial Stability Facility, but may not maintain the same purchasing rate. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA SAYS 3Q INDICATORS WEAK DESPITE STRONGER SEP OUTPUT DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Monday said economic momentum deteriorated during the third quarter despite better-than-expected industrial output growth in September, but reiterated the government will do its best to meet its 2011 economic growth target of 4.5%. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN INFLATION UP 0.1% IN OCTOBER VS SEPTEMBER - TD MI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cheaper fruit and vegetables weren't enough to keep Australian inflation from rising slightly in October, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 -Melbourne Institute monthly inflation gauge showed Monday. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER LI: CHINA INFLATION TO DROP TO 2.8% IN 2012 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer price index growth may drop sharply to 2.8% in 2012, the Beijing Times reported Monday, citing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: LAST WEEK'S EURO-ZONE SUMMIT REDUCED GLOBAL RECESSION WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Monday said the euro-zone agreement on managing the region's debt problems has reduced worries about the risk of a global recession. (published 0038 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA PRESIDENT: G-20 TO DISCUSS WAYS TO STABILIZE, STIMULATE GLOBAL GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders attending the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations summit in Cannes this week will discuss ways to stabilize and stimulate global economic growth, President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono said Monday. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SHANGHAI MUNICIPALITY TO SELL CNY7.1B BONDS IN NOVEMBER - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The municipality of Shanghai plans to directly sell CNY7.1 billion worth of local government debt in November, three people familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOC HONG KONG SEEKS PRICE 5-YEAR DOLLAR BONDS TO YIELD AROUND TSYS +290BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOC Hong Kong Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to price an issuance of five-year, U.S. dollar-denominated bonds at around 290 basis points over comparable Treasurys, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par WSJ: SLOW US RECOVERY FEELS LIKE RECESSION AS DATA PAINT BLEAK PICTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Americans are two years into a recovery that doesn't feel much different to many of them from life during the most bruising recession in seven decades. Scenes of the long haul back from the slump show a nation struggling to rebuild after a battering that crossed ages, regions and occupations. (published 0011 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(10/31) HEARD ON THE ST: WALL STREET REAPS PROFIT VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Here's a pop quiz: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the third quarter generated: a) 56 cents a share in earnings, b) 27 cents, c) a loss of two cents, or d) all of the above. (published 0136 GMT) [ 31-10-11 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111031e7av0007v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
