\par\par \b \uc2 JGBs Fall As BOJ's Additional Easing Falls Short Of Expectations\b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2011\par 08:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                      At 0600 GMT   Change \par    TFX Jun 3-Mos Euroyen Price:        99.670      -0.005 \par    TSE Dec 10-Yr JGB Futures Price:    142.52       -0.14 \par    10-Yr 1.0% JGB No. 318 Yield:       1.010%      +0.020 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese government bonds fell on Thursday as the Bank of Japan's announced additional easing measures fell short of market expectations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 At a one-day policy board meeting that ended earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to expand the size of its asset-purchase program to Y55 trillion from the previous Y50 trillion, and the increase will be made up of buying of JGBs.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ, meanwhile, didn't lengthen the maturity of government debt it buys in the fund, a step that local media reported ahead of the meeting as an option that the BOJ is considering.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said their expectations for lengthening were high, so the overall outcome was somewhat disappointing.\par \par \uc2 "It's not a minus for JGBs, but surely it's not plus to the market. It won't help weakening the yen either," said Atsushi Ito, a senior analyst at UBS Securities.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, investors will pay attention to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will conduct a yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still traded around its record-high levels against the U.S. counterpart.\par \par \uc2 Another focus are coming U.S. economic indicators, they said. If they the figures are worse-than-expected, investor speculation that there may be another quantitative easing program the Fed will increase and support the JGBs in turn.\par \par \uc2 As of 0600 GMT, the two-year yield is down 0.5 basis point to 0.140% due to the BOJ's new measure, while the five-year rose 0.5 basis point to 0.355%. The 10-year is up two basis points to 1.010% and the 20-year is up two basis points to 1.755% and the 30-year is at 1.955%, up 1.5 basis point.\par \par \uc2 The lead JGB futures are down 0.14 to 142.52.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Other Cash Bond Yields            At 0600 GMT   Change \par  \par     2-Year 0.2% JGB No. 310 Yield:      0.140%      -0.005 \par     5-Year 0.4% JGB No. 99 Yield:       0.355%      +0.005 \par     20-Year 1.8% JGB No. 130 Yield:     1.755%      +0.020 \par     30-Year 2.0% JGB No. 35 Yield:      1.955%      +0.015 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 27-10-11 0637GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1037 4153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111027e7ar000jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
