\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 2-BOJ to debate easing with eyes on yen, Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2011\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * BOJ likely to debate easing on Thursday -sources\par \par \uc2  * Finmin repeats warning that ready to act on yen\par \par \uc2  * Prospects dim for clear deal at EU crisis summit\par \par \uc2  * BOJ's JGB buying already huge - Shirakawa \par \par \uc2 (Adds Shirakawa, Azumi quotes)\par \par \uc2  By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan is likely to debate easing monetary policy further at a meeting on Thursday after the yen rose to a record high and doubts mounted over whether Europe can forge a clear plan to tackle the euro zone debt crisis, sources said.\par \par \uc2  If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts, it will likely expand its 50 trillion yen ($660 billion) asset-buying programme by around 5 trillion yen, sources familiar with the bank's thinking said.\par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa, however, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already buying massive amounts of government bonds to keep monetary conditions ultra-easy, countering views it was not doing enough to support the economy and suggesting that an easing on Thursday was hardly a done deal. \par \par \uc2  Japanese policymakers also continued their jawboning to keep markets from pushing up the yen further, although Japan's finance minister acknowledged that rallying G7 support for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen would be tough.\par \par \uc2  "It would be very hard to forge a common interest and conduct joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Finance Minister Jun Azumi told Parliament on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  "We have been saying that in light of Japan's current economic situation, dollar/yen levels of 76 and 77 are inappropriate," he said, signalling that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem sharp yen gains will be unilateral.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy is recovering from the devastating March earthquake and tsunami and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been counting on fiscal spending on reconstruction and demand from emerging markets to sustain the upturn.\par \par \uc2  But the yen's renewed climb to record highs against the dollar are dimming Japan's economic outlook. The increase is being driven largely by safe-haven demand amid concern that Wednesday's European Union crisis summit will fail to produce a decisive solution.\par \par \uc2  Many central bankers have hoped to save their limited policy options for later, the sources told Reuters, but in light of the latest market jitters the decision will be a close call. The BOJ will scrutinise the outcome of Wednesday's summit of European leaders, and its market fallout, in determining whether to act now rather than later. \par \par \uc2  SPECULATORS WARNED\par \par \uc2  The BOJ last eased policy by boosting its asset buying pool in August, acting in tandem with the finance ministry which ordered \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest-ever single-day \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling more than 4.5 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2  The impact, however, proved short-lived and the yen crawled back to trade close to its record highs.\par \par \uc2  This has been a source of deepening frustration for Japanese officials, who argue that a yen rally is one problem too many for a nation grappling with a nuclear crisis, a $250 billion post-quake rebuilding effort and ballooning debt.\par \par \uc2  The yen's break to new peaks against the dollar last Friday and again on Tuesday prompted warnings from Japanese authorities that Tokyo was ready to step in to stem yen rises.\par \par \uc2  Azumi on Wednesday served dealers another warning after the yen climbed to 75.73 to the dollar in New York the previous day, saying he would not rule out any steps to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation and had instructed staff to be prepared for all possible measures on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  He also hinted at possible concerted action with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "The BOJ shares our sense of crisis, so I'm sure they will take appropriate steps when necessary," Azumi told reporters.\par \par \uc2  Expectations of BOJ easing pushed up Japanese government bond prices, while caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the yen hovering around 76.10 to the dollar in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2  But analysts doubt whether Tokyo is ready to sell yen at a big enough size to turn the tide.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible if dollar/yen falls to a new post-war low, but it would be a small amount of money," said Junya Tanase, chief strategist at \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't that willing to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of agreements with the G7. The comments officials are making today are more verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and may not have much meaning for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy."\par \par \uc2  The prospects for a comprehensive deal to resolve the euro zone debt crisis this week appear dim, with deep disagreement remaining on critical elements, including how to give the region's bailout fund greater firepower. \par \par \uc2  Investors fear that without a clear solution, the sovereign debt crisis engulfing highly indebted nations of the euro zone periphery could trigger a banking crisis and a credit crunch similar to what followed the \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  collapse in 2008.\par \par \uc2  Since September 2010, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice on its own and once jointly with other G7 rich nations to weaken the yen. But the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have proved fleeting in the face of steady demand from nervous investors seeking highly liquid and relatively safe assets such as Japanese government bonds.\par \par \uc2  ($1 = 75.770 Japanese yen) \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Stanley White, Rie Ishiguro and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Writing by Tomasz Janowski and Leika Kihara; Editing by Edmund Klamann and Matt Driskill)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/(WRAPUP 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111029e7aq0000z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
