\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 24\b0\par\par\uc2 1,762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2011\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN HARDENS RHETORIC AFTER YEN HITS POST-WAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister on Monday ratcheted up his warnings against the strong yen, helping to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar by raising the specter of renewed yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Tokyo. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE:\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  EXPORTS, TRADE SURPLUS RECOVER TO PRE-QUAKE LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese exports and the country's trade surplus have now recovered all their losses since the March earthquake and tsunami, though the yen's record strength, the European debt crisis and slower growth overseas threaten the economy's recovery from the disasters. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRELIMINARY CHINA PMI REBOUNDS TO 51.1 IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The preliminary HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index, a gauge of nationwide manufacturing activity, rebounded strongly in October, rising to 51.1 from a final reading of 49.9 in September, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA INTEREST-RATE SWAPS ACTIVITY SUGGESTS RATE CUT EXPECTED WITHIN 12 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading activity in China's interest-rate swap market suggests market participants expect the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower its benchmark interest rates over the next 12 months, reversing a monetary tightening cycle that started a year ago. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STATE ECONOMIST: ECONOMIC GROWTH RATE MAY BE ABOVE 9% IN 2011 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy is likely to expand by more than 9% this year, and growth should remain reasonable despite the recent slowdown, an economist with a government think-tank wrote in an article published by the state-run People's Daily on Monday. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA OFFICIAL: INFLATION TO FALL BELOW 5% BY NOVEMBER - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer price growth will fall below 5% in November and December, a top economic planning official was cited as saying Monday, offering confidence that the government may have gained the upper hand in its fight against inflation. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: STATE STREET GLOBAL ADVISORS: LIQUIDITY LIMITS GLOBAL INTEREST IN YUAN ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The still-thin liquidity of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  outside its borders is a key barrier for global investors who are showing "a genuine interest" in investing in assets linked to the yuan, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Scott Powers\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of the investment arm of \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Street Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BENIGN AUSTRALIAN PPI DATA BRINGS RATE CUT CLOSER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An interest rate cut in Australia moved a small step closer Monday as producer price inflation proved more benign than expected in the third quarter. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TO OFFER BANKS INCENTIVES TO SUPPORT SMALL FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator said Monday it will offer incentives to encourage banks to boost their financial support for cash-hungry small businesses. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE CPI INFLATION EASES A BIT; VINDICATES EASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer prices rose more slowly than expected in September as the pace of increase in transportation, clothing and recreation costs eased, vindicating the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to ease monetary policy. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: THAI FLOODS LIKELY TO COST THAILAND 2% OF 2011 GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flooding in Thailand is likely to cost 2% of the country's 2011 gross domestic product, but the government has ample fiscal space to absorb related expenses, reports by Moody's Investors Service found Monday. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM OCTOBER CPI UP 0.36% ON MONTH, UP 21.59% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index rose 0.36% on month in October, slower than a 0.82% rise in September and an increase of 0.93% in August, the government's General Statistics Office said Monday. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA PLANS TO RELEASE REBASED INFLATION DATA IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "With the planned change of the base year to 2010 from 2005, we're going to apply a new standard to the consumer price index as some items are newly added while some other items are excluded," said an official at Statistics Korea. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR LITTLE CHANGED VS YEN ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was little changed against the yen on Monday in Asia as heightened caution over possible market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept investors away from active trading. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH: HK BANKS COULD FACE RATINGS DOWNGRADES ON CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong banks with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in mainland China could face ratings downgrades in the coming months, as there are concerns that slowing economic growth and deteriorating asset quality in the country could impact their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Fitch Ratings said Monday. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  UPS 1H GROUP NET PROFIT VIEW TO Y10.60B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday raised its earnings forecast for the six months ended Sept. 30 due to higher volumes of auto sales and cost reductions. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: EX NEWCREST HEAD IAN SMITH TO TAKE OVER AS ORICA CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Newcrest Mining Ltd. Chief Executive Ian Smith will take over from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Graeme Liebelt\f28 \uc2 \f2  as chief executive of chemicals group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Orica Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . next February, the company said Monday. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASCIANO REFINANCES $1.44B IN BANK FACILITIES, CUTS RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian infrastructure group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asciano Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it had refinanced its A$1.44 billion debt facilities at a lower interest rate and with a smaller number of banks. (published 2146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PROSERPINE GROWER VOTE ON WILMAR OFFER TO CLOSE THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Grower members of the troubled Proserpine Cooperative Sugar Milling Association Ltd. will vote this week on a takeover offer by the giant of the Australian sugar industry, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wilmar International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Sucrogen unit, with one of Australia's last independently owned sugar cane mills at stake as consolidation of the local industry continues. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHARMAXIS GETS THE NOD FOR CYSTIC FIBROSIS DRUG IN EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pharmaxis Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has been cleared by the Committee for Medicinal Products for Human Use to market its Bronchitol drug to help treat adults with cystic fibrosis in Europe, and the company expects the European Commission to confirm this decision in January 2012. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OLYMPUS: CHANGED AUDITORS AS CONTRACT FOR PREVIOUS AUDITOR EXPIRED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday denied media reports that said its former auditing firm, KPMG AZSA LLC, quit being the Japanese company's auditor because of accounting issues relating to the 2008 acquisition of the U.K.'s Gyrus Group Ltd. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: OLYMPUS DEALS FACED SCRUTINY AT THE COMPANY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The deals at the center of a controversy surrounding Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . were the subject of internal scrutiny more than two years ago, according to documents viewed by The Wall Street Journal. published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINAVISION TO ACQUIRE FILM DISTRIBUTOR, SELL STAKE TO TENCENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ChinaVision Media Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it will acquire a Chinese film distribution company for HK$2.016 billion, and also introduce \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tencent Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as a strategic investor. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA'S NEW TAKEOVER RULES COME INTO FORCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New takeover rules that increase the trigger for compulsory open offers and raise the minimum offer size have come into effect from Oct. 22, an executive of India's capital market regulator said Monday. (published 0539 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK NIAGA JAN-SEPT NET PROFIT UP 33% AT IDR2.378 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank CIMB Niaga\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday its net profit for the January-to-September period was IDR2.378 trillion, up 33% from IDR1.794 trillion a year earlier, due to higher net interest and fee-based income. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SECURITY BANK SECURES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OK FOR REGULAR, BONUS CASH DIVIDEND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Security Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday the Philippines' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  approved its recently declared regular and bonus cash dividends. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KIM ENG HOLDINGS TO BEGIN TENDER OFFER FOR ATR KIMENG SHARES OCT. 27 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ATR KimEng Financial Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that its biggest shareholder, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Eng Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., will make a tender offer for all the shares of the Manila-listed financial institution. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY LOWER AS EU DEBT TALKS STUMBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower in choppy trade Friday and the euro treaded water, as sentiment was weighed by concerns Europe's efforts to deliver a comprehensive plan to resolve the euro-zone debt crisis might unravel. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: RIO TINTO LONG-TERM DEMAND OUTLOOK UNCHANGED -CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The long-term demand outlook for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's metals and minerals is unchanged, despite a volatile macro environment, Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Albanese\f28 \uc2 \f2  told analysts Monday. (published 0333 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DATA: CHINA CONFIRMS SEPTEMBER CRUDE IMPORTS DOWN 12.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's General Administration of Customs confirmed Monday that September crude-oil imports totaled 20.45 million metric tons, equivalent to almost 5 million barrels a day, down 12.2% from a year earlier. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: OIL DATA: JAPAN SEPTEMBER LNG IMPORTS UP, CRUDE DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's crude-oil imports fell in September, despite the country's increased reliance on thermal power to make up for idled nuclear capacity. Liquefied natural gas has accounted for most of the country's extra fossil fuel demand in the aftermath of the March 11 earthquake and tsunami. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 2011-12 WHEAT FORECAST RAISED; PROTEIN CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While Australia's wheat crop looks set for near record production this year, significant doubts are emerging about relatively low protein levels in early-harvest grain. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S AWB CUTS ESTIMATED RETURNS ON 2011-12 WHEAT CROP SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 24-10-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia-based wheat exporter \f28 \uc2 \f2 AWB Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cargill Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Monday revised estimated returns on collective sales of most wheat from the 2011-12 crop, citing recent heavy falls in U.S. wheat futures. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PROSERPINE GROWER VOTE ON WILMAR OFFER TO CLOSE THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Grower members of the troubled Proserpine Cooperative Sugar Milling Association Ltd. will vote this week on a takeover offer by the giant of the Australian sugar industry, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wilmar International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Sucrogen unit, with one of Australia's last independently owned sugar cane mills at stake as consolidation of the local industry continues. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA CUTS CPO, COCOA EXPORT TAXES TO 15%, 5% FOR NOVEMBER VS 16.5%, 10% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government has cut the tax imposed on crude palm oil for November to 15% from 16.5% in October, a government official said Monday. (published 0120 GMT) [ 24-10-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111024e7ao000ho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
