\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: USD/JPY To Consolidate\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2011\par 02:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0724 [Dow Jones] USD/JPY - to consolidate after hitting record low 75.78 on EBS Friday as markets realized Japan's Y12 trillion package of measures is meant to cope with, not combat, the strong JPY. USD/JPY also undermined by Japan exporter sales, negative USD sentiment (ICE spot dollar index last 76.48 vs 76.93 early Friday) after Fed Vice Chairman Yellen offered gloomy assessment of U.S. economy and hinted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be moving toward third round of securities purchases to revive economy. But USD/JPY downside limited by Japan importer demand, heightened expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Finance Minister Azumi promises "resolute action" against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. USD/JPY also cushioned by reduced safe-haven appeal of yen and yen-funded carry trades as global risk sentiment improves (VIX fear gauge eased 9.95% to 31.32; DJIA rose 2.31%) on hopes that Europe's leaders will unveil comprehensive plan to resolve region's debt crisis on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  Yen crosses vulnerable to 0230 GMT October HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI data. Data focus: 2350 GMT Japan September provisional trade statistics, 1230 GMT U.S. September Chicago Fed national activity index, 1245 GMT Fed's Dudley speaks, 1300 GMT Fed's Fisher speaks. 1900 GMT Fed's Yellen speech. USD/JPY daily chart negative-biased as MACD & stochastics in bearish mode; bearish parabolic stop-and-reverse signal hit at 76.52 Friday. Support at 75.78 (Friday's low); breach would expose downside to psychological 75.00 and 74.00 levels, then 73.13 (projected base of descending channel formed with the April 2009 high of 101.45 and Nov. 2009 low of 84.81 on weekly chart). Resistance at 76.60 (hourly chart), then at 76.92 (Friday's high) and 77.10 (Thursday's high); breach would target 77.46-77.49 (Oct. 17 high-Oct. 12 high), then 77.59 (Sept. 12 high), 77.86 (Sept. 9 high) and 78.02 (100-day moving average).\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020111025e7ao00453\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdr